PathwayData.put("data/reading_writing/units/L06U6.json",{"strand":"reading_writing","level":6,"cefr":"B1b","unit":6,"theme":"Making a Difference","essential_question":"How can one person make a difference?","schema_version":"1.0","core_words":["campaign","cause","fundraiser","awareness","contribute","organize","initiative","impact","participate","benefit","encourage","community","target","citizen"],"recycled_words":["help","volunteer","community","theme","character","problem","solution","persuade","formal","request","because","in addition","would"],"rubrics":[{"id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","title":"Analytic writing rubric","traits":[{"name":"Ideas","name_ar":"الأفكار","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear, interesting and fully developed with strong details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة وممتعة ومدعومة بتفاصيل قوية."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear and have enough details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة ومعها تفاصيل كافية."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"My main idea is there but needs more details.","descriptor_ar":"فكرتي الرئيسية موجودة لكنها تحتاج إلى تفاصيل أكثر."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"My ideas are unclear or very few.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري غير واضحة أو قليلة جدًا."}]},{"name":"Organization","name_ar":"التنظيم","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Clear beginning, middle and end; ideas flow with linking words.","descriptor_ar":"بداية ووسط ونهاية واضحة، والأفكار مترابطة بكلمات الربط."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Clear order with some linking words.","descriptor_ar":"ترتيب واضح مع بعض كلمات الربط."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Some order, but parts are mixed up.","descriptor_ar":"يوجد بعض الترتيب لكن بعض الأجزاء غير مرتبة."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Ideas are not in order.","descriptor_ar":"الأفكار غير مرتبة."}]},{"name":"Vocabulary","name_ar":"المفردات","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"I use exact, varied words, including new unit words, correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات دقيقة ومتنوعة، منها كلمات الوحدة الجديدة، بشكل صحيح."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"I use some new words correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم بعض الكلمات الجديدة بشكل صحيح."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"I use simple words; some are repeated or wrong.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات بسيطة، وبعضها مكرر أو غير صحيح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"I use very few words; the meaning is hard to understand.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات قليلة جدًا ويصعب فهم المعنى."}]},{"name":"Sentence fluency","name_ar":"سلاسة الجمل","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My sentences are complete, varied in length and easy to read aloud.","descriptor_ar":"جملي كاملة ومتنوعة الطول وسهلة القراءة بصوت عالٍ."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Most sentences are complete, with some variety.","descriptor_ar":"معظم جملي كاملة مع بعض التنويع."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Many sentences are short or start the same way.","descriptor_ar":"كثير من جملي قصيرة أو تبدأ بالطريقة نفسها."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Sentences are incomplete or run together.","descriptor_ar":"جملي ناقصة أو متداخلة."}]},{"name":"Conventions","name_ar":"قواعد الكتابة","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Capitals, punctuation, spelling and grammar are almost always correct.","descriptor_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة وعلامات الترقيم والإملاء والقواعد صحيحة دائمًا تقريبًا."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"A few mistakes that do not affect meaning.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء قليلة لا تؤثر في المعنى."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Several mistakes; the meaning is sometimes unclear.","descriptor_ar":"عدة أخطاء، والمعنى أحيانًا غير واضح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Many mistakes make it hard to read.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء كثيرة تجعل القراءة صعبة."}]}]}],"lessons":[{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS1","title":"Word Power: Making a Difference","lesson_type":"vocabulary","objectives":["read, say and use 14 words about making a difference and 4 Tier 2 words (propose, approve, request, collaborate)","understand and use idioms about helping (lend a hand, make a difference, pitch in, go the extra mile)","decide when idioms fit (friendly writing) and when to avoid them (formal letters)"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة ونطق واستخدام 14 كلمة عن صنع الفرق و4 كلمات أكاديمية.","فهم التعابير الاصطلاحية عن المساعدة واستخدامها.","تحديد متى تناسب التعابير الاصطلاحية (الكتابة الودية) ومتى نتجنبها (الرسائل الرسمية)."],"success_criteria":["I can use the community words correctly in sentences.","I can explain the real meaning of six helping idioms.","I can replace an idiom with a formal phrase for a letter."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع استخدام كلمات المجتمع في جمل بشكل صحيح.","أستطيع شرح المعنى الحقيقي لستة تعابير عن المساعدة.","أستطيع استبدال التعبير الاصطلاحي بعبارة رسمية في الرسالة."],"map_area":"Vocabulary: Acquisition and Use","vocabulary":[{"word":"campaign","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kæmˈpeɪn/","definition":"a planned group of activities to achieve a goal","arabic":"حملة","example":"We started a campaign to clean the beach.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"cause","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɔz/","definition":"an idea or a group that people support and work for","arabic":"قضية / هدف نبيل","example":"Helping orphans is an important cause.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"fundraiser","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfʌndˌreɪzər/","definition":"an event to collect money for a cause","arabic":"فعالية لجمع التبرعات","example":"Our bake sale was a successful fundraiser.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"awareness","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈwɛrnəs/","definition":"knowing about a problem or a situation","arabic":"وعي / توعية","example":"The posters raised awareness about saving water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"contribute","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈtrɪbjut/","definition":"to give money, time or help to a shared goal","arabic":"يسهم","example":"Everyone can contribute something.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"organize","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈɔrɡəˌnaɪz/","definition":"to plan and arrange an event or activity","arabic":"ينظّم","example":"Dana organized a meeting with the principal.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"initiative","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪˈnɪʃətɪv/","definition":"a new plan to solve a problem; the ability to start things yourself","arabic":"مبادرة","example":"The rooftop garden was a student initiative.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V07","tier":"core"},{"word":"impact","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɪmˌpækt/","definition":"a strong effect on something or someone","arabic":"أثر","example":"The garden had a big impact on our school.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V08","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V08","tier":"core"},{"word":"participate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/pɑrˈtɪsəˌpeɪt/","definition":"to take part in an activity","arabic":"يشارك","example":"Forty students participated in the clean-up.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V09","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V09","tier":"core"},{"word":"benefit","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/ˈbɛnəfɪt/","definition":"a good result or advantage; to help someone","arabic":"فائدة / يفيد","example":"The garden benefits the whole school.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V10","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V10","tier":"core"},{"word":"encourage","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɪnˈkɝɪdʒ/","definition":"to give someone hope and confidence to do something","arabic":"يشجّع","example":"Her teacher encouraged her to continue.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V11","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V11","tier":"core"},{"word":"community","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈmjunəti/","definition":"the people who live in one area or share something","arabic":"مجتمع","example":"The whole community helped.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V12","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V12","tier":"core"},{"word":"target","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtɑrɡɪt/","definition":"a goal or an amount you want to reach","arabic":"هدف (رقم مستهدف)","example":"Our target is to raise 2,000 riyals.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V13","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V13","tier":"core"},{"word":"citizen","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɪtəzən/","definition":"a person who belongs to a country or a city and has rights and duties there","arabic":"مواطن","example":"A good citizen cares for the community.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V14","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V14","tier":"core"},{"word":"propose","pos":"verb","ipa":"/prəˈpoʊz/","definition":"to suggest a plan for others to consider","arabic":"يقترح","example":"I propose a reading buddies program.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V15","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V15","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"approve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əˈpruv/","definition":"to officially agree to a plan","arabic":"يوافق على / يعتمد","example":"The principal approved our garden project.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V16","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V16","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"request","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/rɪˈkwɛst/","definition":"a polite act of asking for something; to ask politely","arabic":"طلب / يطلب","example":"We sent a formal request to the council.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V17","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V17","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"collaborate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈlæbəˌreɪt/","definition":"to work together with others to produce something","arabic":"يتعاون","example":"Students and parents collaborated on the project.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V18","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V18","tier":"tier2"}],"explanation":{"text":"An **idiom** is a group of words whose meaning is **different from the meanings of the separate words**. *Lend a hand* doesn't mean giving someone your hand to keep! It means **help**. You can't translate idioms word for word – you have to **learn their meaning** and **use the context**.\n\nHelping idioms: **lend a hand** = help; **make a difference** = have a good effect; **pitch in** = join in and help with a job; **go the extra mile** = do more than you have to; **many hands make light work** = a job is easy when many people help; **every little bit helps** = even small help is useful; **roll up your sleeves** = get ready to work hard; **give back** = help the community that helped you.\n\nIdioms make **friendly** speech and stories lively. But in **formal writing** – like a letter to the principal – use **plain, formal words** instead: *pitch in* → ***participate***; *lend a hand* → ***assist***; *make a difference* → ***have a positive impact***.","examples":["***Lend a hand:*** *Can you lend a hand with these boxes?* = Can you help?","***Make a difference:*** *One small idea can make a difference.* = have a good effect.","***Pitch in:*** *Everyone pitched in to clean the playground.* = joined in and helped.","***Go the extra mile:*** *Our coach goes the extra mile for every player.* = does more than necessary.","***Many hands make light work:*** *With forty volunteers, we finished in an hour – many hands make light work!*","***Every little bit helps:*** *Even one riyal is useful – every little bit helps.*","***Roll up your sleeves:*** *Let's roll up our sleeves and start planting.* = get ready to work hard.","***Give back:*** *After university, she wanted to give back to her hometown.* = help the community.","Formal letter: not *pitch in* but → *We hope many students will **participate**.*"],"common_errors":["✗ Translating an idiom word for word. → ✓ Learn the whole meaning: lend a hand = help. (Idioms are not literal.)","✗ Can you borrow me a hand? → ✓ Can you lend me a hand? (lend (give), not borrow.)","✗ She did a difference. → ✓ She made a difference. (**make** a difference.)","✗ Dear Principal, everyone will pitch in! → ✓ Dear Principal, many students will participate. (Formal letter → formal words.)","✗ He went the extra kilometer. → ✓ He went the extra mile. (Don't change the words of an idiom.)","✗ The community are helping. → ✓ The community is helping. (community = singular (American English).)","✗ Using five idioms in one paragraph. → ✓ Use one or two where they fit. (Don't overuse idioms.)"],"arabic":"التعبير الاصطلاحي مجموعة كلمات معناها مختلف عن معاني كلماتها المنفردة، فـ lend a hand لا تعني أن تعطي يدك بل تعني «يساعد»، ولا يُترجم حرفيًا.\n\nتعابير المساعدة: lend a hand (يساعد)، make a difference (يُحدث فرقًا)، pitch in (يشارك في العمل)، go the extra mile (يبذل أكثر من المطلوب)، many hands make light work (اليد الواحدة لا تصفق)، every little bit helps (كل مساعدة مهما صغرت مفيدة).\n\nالتعابير تجعل الحديث الودي والقصص حيوية، أما في الكتابة الرسمية كرسالة إلى المدير فاستخدم كلمات رسمية: participate بدل pitch in، وassist بدل lend a hand.\n\nانتبه: نقول make a difference لا do a difference، وlend me a hand لا borrow me a hand."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:30","narration":"An empty roof. A big idea. A whole school ready to help. Can one person make a difference?","on_screen":"Making a Difference 🌱🤝","visual":"A bare school roof transforms into a green garden in time-lapse."},{"time":"00:30–01:30","narration":"Campaign, cause, fundraiser, awareness, contribute, organize, initiative, impact, participate, benefit, encourage, community, target, citizen!","on_screen":"campaign · cause · fundraiser · awareness · contribute · organize · initiative · impact · participate · benefit · encourage · community · target · citizen","visual":"Each word appears on a volunteer badge."},{"time":"01:30–02:05","narration":"Propose a plan, request permission, collaborate with others – and wait for the principal to approve!","on_screen":"propose · request · collaborate · approve","visual":"A student hands a letter to a principal who stamps APPROVED."},{"time":"02:05–03:30","narration":"Lend a hand, make a difference, pitch in, go the extra mile – many hands make light work!","on_screen":"Helping idioms","visual":"Cartoon hands literally lend, pitch and roll up sleeves – then the real meanings appear."},{"time":"03:30–04:00","narration":"Idioms are great in stories – but in a formal letter, choose formal words!","on_screen":"Friendly: pitch in · Formal: participate","visual":"A letter changes 'pitch in' to 'participate'."}],"captions_ar":["سطح فارغ، وفكرة كبيرة، ومدرسة كاملة مستعدة للمساعدة. هل يستطيع شخص واحد أن يُحدث فرقًا؟","حملة، قضية، فعالية تبرعات، وعي، يسهم، ينظّم، مبادرة، أثر، يشارك، فائدة، يشجّع، مجتمع، هدف، مواطن!","اقترح خطة، واطلب الإذن، وتعاون مع الآخرين، وانتظر موافقة المدير!","مدّ يد العون، أحدث فرقًا، شارك، ابذل أكثر، فاليد الواحدة لا تصفق!","التعابير رائعة في القصص، أما في الرسالة الرسمية فاختر كلمات رسمية!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm, encouraging female voice, speed 1.0."},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct community word.","instructions_ar":"اختر كلمة المجتمع الصحيحة.","items":[{"q":"Our bake sale raised 1,500 riyals for the children's hospital. It was a great ___.","answer":"fundraiser","explanation":"Fundraiser.","explanation_ar":"فعالية تبرعات.","options":["citizen","fundraiser","target","impact"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"The posters in the hallway raised ___ about saving water.","answer":"awareness","explanation":"Awareness.","explanation_ar":"الوعي.","options":["fundraiser","citizen","approval","awareness"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Forty students ___ in the beach clean-up on Saturday.","answer":"participated","explanation":"Participate.","explanation_ar":"شاركوا.","options":["approved","proposed","participated","requested"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Our ___ is to collect 500 books for the village library.","answer":"target","explanation":"Target.","explanation_ar":"هدفنا.","options":["citizen","campaign","benefit","target"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"The new reading corner had a big ___ on how much the younger students read.","answer":"impact","explanation":"Impact.","explanation_ar":"أثر.","options":["impact","request","citizen","cause"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Starting the garden without being asked showed real ___.","answer":"initiative","explanation":"Initiative.","explanation_ar":"مبادرة.","options":["initiative","awareness","fundraiser","target"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS1-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Idioms about helping. Choose.","instructions_ar":"تعابير المساعدة: اختر.","items":[{"q":"*Could you **lend a hand** with these chairs?* What does the speaker want?","answer":"help","explanation":"Idiom.","explanation_ar":"المساعدة.","options":["a glove","money","help","a handshake"],"dok":1,"skill":"idioms","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Everyone **pitched in**, so the classroom was clean in ten minutes.* What does *pitched in* mean?","answer":"joined in and helped","explanation":"Idiom.","explanation_ar":"شارك وساعد.","options":["threw things","sat down","joined in and helped","went home"],"dok":2,"skill":"idioms","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Mr. Khalid always **goes the extra mile** for his students.* What does this mean?","answer":"He does more than he has to.","explanation":"Idiom.","explanation_ar":"يبذل أكثر من المطلوب.","options":["He walks a long way.","He does more than he has to.","He drives fast.","He is often late."],"dok":2,"skill":"idioms","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which idiom about volunteers is used correctly?","answer":"Our volunteers made a big difference to the hospital.","explanation":"make a difference.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Our volunteers did a big difference to the hospital.","Our volunteers took a big difference to the hospital.","Our volunteers had a big difference to the hospital.","Our volunteers made a big difference to the hospital."],"dok":2,"skill":"idioms","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which idiom matches the Arabic proverb *اليد الواحدة لا تصفق*?","answer":"Many hands make light work.","explanation":"Meaning.","explanation_ar":"Many hands make light work.","options":["Many hands make light work.","Roll up your sleeves.","Every little bit helps.","Go the extra mile."],"dok":2,"skill":"idioms","stage":"guided"},{"q":"In a FORMAL letter to the principal, which phrase should replace *pitch in*?","answer":"participate","explanation":"Formal language.","explanation_ar":"participate.","options":["lend a hand","participate","roll up our sleeves","go the extra mile"],"dok":3,"skill":"formal language","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS1-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the word bank. Each word fits one sentence.","instructions_ar":"استخدم بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"I would like to ________ a new reading buddies program.","answer":"propose","explanation":"Suggest a plan.","explanation_ar":"أقترح.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"We hope the principal will ________ our plan this week.","answer":"approve","explanation":"Agree officially.","explanation_ar":"يوافق على.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Our class sent a formal ________ for permission to use the roof.","answer":"request","explanation":"Polite asking.","explanation_ar":"طلبًا.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Students and parents will ________ to build the garden beds.","answer":"collaborate","explanation":"Work together.","explanation_ar":"يتعاونون.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Every citizen can ________ something to the community: time, money or ideas.","answer":"contribute","explanation":"Give.","explanation_ar":"يسهم.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Dana ________ a meeting with the school council.","answer":"organized","explanation":"Planned.","explanation_ar":"نظّمت.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS1-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write with the new words.","instructions_ar":"اكتب باستخدام الكلمات الجديدة.","items":[{"q":"Write two sentences with idioms about a time you helped someone.","answer":"Last Eid, I lent a hand to my grandmother in the kitchen. Everyone pitched in, and we finished cooking quickly.","explanation":"Idioms.","explanation_ar":"التعابير.","dok":2,"skill":"idioms","stage":"production"},{"q":"Rewrite this sentence for a formal letter: *Everyone will pitch in and lend a hand.*","answer":"Many students will participate and assist with the project.","explanation":"Formal.","explanation_ar":"رسمي.","dok":2,"skill":"formal language","stage":"production"},{"q":"Describe a campaign you would like to organize at your school. What is its target?","answer":"I would like to organize a campaign to collect winter clothes for families in need. Our target is 300 jackets.","explanation":"Plan.","explanation_ar":"خطّط.","dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"production"},{"q":"Do you think one person can really make a difference? Explain with an example.","answer":"Yes, because one person can start an initiative that encourages others to join – for example, one student's idea for a recycling bin can change a whole school's habits.","explanation":"Opinion.","explanation_ar":"رأي.","dok":3,"skill":"reasoning","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Idiom Charades and Swap","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Act and swap: an avatar acts out an idiom literally; the child chooses the real meaning, then swaps the idiom in a formal letter for the right formal word. Each correct swap earns a 'community helper' badge.","A player draws an idiom card and acts out its LITERAL meaning (for example, rolling up sleeves).","The team guesses the idiom and its real meaning.","Then the team chooses the formal word that could replace it in a letter.","Correct idiom = 1 point; real meaning = 1 point; formal swap = 1 point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Which word means *a planned group of activities to achieve a goal*?","answer":"campaign","explanation":"Campaign.","explanation_ar":"حملة.","options":["citizen","campaign","benefit","target"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"What is an *idiom*?","answer":"a group of words whose meaning is different from the separate words","explanation":"Definition.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي.","options":["a very long word","a word with a prefix","a kind of letter","a group of words whose meaning is different from the separate words"],"dok":1,"skill":"idioms"},{"q":"*The principal **approved** our project.* *Approved* means ___.","answer":"officially agreed to","explanation":"Context.","explanation_ar":"وافق على.","options":["refused","forgot","changed","officially agreed to"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"What does *make a difference* mean?","answer":"have a good effect","explanation":"Idiom.","explanation_ar":"يُحدث فرقًا.","options":["change your clothes","see two things","have a good effect","make a list"],"dok":1,"skill":"idioms"},{"q":"Which sentence about the community is correct?","answer":"The community is helping to build the garden.","explanation":"community = singular.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["The community are helping to build the garden yesterday.","The community helping to build the garden.","The community is helping to build the garden.","The community is help to build the garden."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"*Even one riyal is useful – **every little bit helps**.* What does the idiom mean?","answer":"Even small help is valuable.","explanation":"Idiom.","explanation_ar":"كل مساعدة مهما صغرت مفيدة.","options":["Even small help is valuable.","Only big donations matter.","Money is not important.","Bits of paper are helpful."],"dok":2,"skill":"idioms"},{"q":"Where are idioms LEAST suitable?","answer":"in a formal letter to the school council","explanation":"Formal vs. friendly.","explanation_ar":"الرسالة الرسمية.","options":["in a formal letter to the school council","in a story about friends","in a chat with a classmate","in a funny poem"],"dok":2,"skill":"formal language"},{"q":"Which phrase is the FORMAL way to say *lend a hand*?","answer":"assist","explanation":"Formal.","explanation_ar":"assist.","options":["pitch in","assist","roll up your sleeves","give a hand away"],"dok":2,"skill":"formal language"},{"q":"*After she became a doctor, she returned to her village to **give back**.* What does *give back* mean here?","answer":"help the community that helped her","explanation":"Idiom in context.","explanation_ar":"ردّ الجميل للمجتمع.","options":["return a borrowed book","give money back to a shop","go back home to sleep","help the community that helped her"],"dok":3,"skill":"idioms"},{"q":"Why can't you translate idioms word for word?","answer":"Their meaning is different from the meanings of the separate words.","explanation":"Strategy.","explanation_ar":"لأن معناها مختلف عن معاني كلماتها.","options":["They are always very short.","They only exist in Arabic.","Their meaning is different from the meanings of the separate words.","They have no meaning."],"dok":3,"skill":"idioms"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'campaign': students holding posters for a cause"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'cause': a heart with hands around it"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'fundraiser': a table with cakes and a money box"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'awareness': a poster with a water drop and an eye"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'contribute': hands putting items into a box"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'organize': a student with a clipboard and a checklist"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'initiative': a student raising a hand with a lightbulb"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V08","prompt":"Picture for the word 'impact': ripples spreading on water"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V09","prompt":"Picture for the word 'participate': students joining hands in a circle"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V10","prompt":"Picture for the word 'benefit': a plus sign on a green leaf"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V11","prompt":"Picture for the word 'encourage': a teacher giving a thumbs-up"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V12","prompt":"Picture for the word 'community': neighbors working together in a street"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V13","prompt":"Picture for the word 'target': a target board with an arrow in the center"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V14","prompt":"Picture for the word 'citizen': a family under a national flag"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V15","prompt":"Picture for the word 'propose': a student presenting a plan to a group"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V16","prompt":"Picture for the word 'approve': a stamp saying APPROVED"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V17","prompt":"Picture for the word 'request': a letter with 'Request' at the top"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V18","prompt":"Picture for the word 'collaborate': people building something together"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-01","prompt":"Students working together on a rooftop garden."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-02","prompt":"Icons for community words."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS1-03","prompt":"Literal and real meanings of helping idioms."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V01","script":"campaign. We started a campaign to clean the beach."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V02","script":"cause. Helping orphans is an important cause."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V03","script":"fundraiser. Our bake sale was a successful fundraiser."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V04","script":"awareness. The posters raised awareness about saving water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V05","script":"contribute. Everyone can contribute something."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V06","script":"organize. Dana organized a meeting with the principal."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V07","script":"initiative. The rooftop garden was a student initiative."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V08","script":"impact. The garden had a big impact on our school."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V09","script":"participate. Forty students participated in the clean-up."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V10","script":"benefit. The garden benefits the whole school."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V11","script":"encourage. Her teacher encouraged her to continue."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V12","script":"community. The whole community helped."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V13","script":"target. Our target is to raise 2,000 riyals."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V14","script":"citizen. A good citizen cares for the community."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V15","script":"propose. I propose a reading buddies program."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V16","script":"approve. The principal approved our garden project."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V17","script":"request. We sent a formal request to the council."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-V18","script":"collaborate. Students and parents collaborated on the project."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS1-VID","script":"An empty roof. A big idea. A whole school ready to help. Can one person make a difference? Campaign, cause, fundraiser, awareness, contribute, organize, initiative, impact, participate, benefit, encourage, community, target, citizen! Propose a plan, request permission, collaborate with others – and wait for the principal to approve! Lend a hand, make a difference, pitch in, go the extra mile – many hands make light work! Idioms are great in stories – but in a formal letter, choose formal words!"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS2","title":"The Garden on the Roof","lesson_type":"close_reading","objectives":["read a realistic story of about 460 words about a student who starts a rooftop garden","analyze how the main character responds to obstacles and how other characters change","explain the problem, the obstacles, the solutions and the impact on the community"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة قصة واقعية من نحو 460 كلمة عن طالبة بدأت حديقة على السطح.","تحليل كيف تتعامل الشخصية الرئيسية مع العقبات وكيف تتغير الشخصيات الأخرى.","شرح المشكلة والعقبات والحلول والأثر في المجتمع."],"success_criteria":["I can list the principal's three questions and the solution to each.","I can describe how Dana and Hessa change, with evidence.","I can explain the impact of the garden using details from the text."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع ذكر أسئلة المديرة الثلاثة وحل كل منها.","أستطيع وصف كيف تغيّرت دانة وحصة بالدليل.","أستطيع شرح أثر الحديقة بتفاصيل من النص."],"map_area":"Literary Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"obstacle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɑbstəkəl/","definition":"something that makes it hard to do what you want","arabic":"عقبة","example":"Water was the biggest obstacle.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"budget","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbʌdʒɪt/","definition":"a plan for how much money you will spend","arabic":"ميزانية","example":"Dana's plan included a budget.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"railing","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈreɪlɪŋ/","definition":"a fence of bars that stops people from falling","arabic":"درابزين","example":"A new safety railing was built on the roof.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"donate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈdoʊˌneɪt/","definition":"to give something to help others","arabic":"يتبرّع","example":"A store donated soil for the garden.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"planter","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈplæntər/","definition":"a large container for growing plants","arabic":"حوض زراعة","example":"Parents built wooden planters.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"herb","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɝb/","definition":"a plant whose leaves are used to add flavor, such as mint or basil","arabic":"عُشبة عطرية","example":"The garden grew fresh herbs.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"give up","pos":"phrasal verb","ipa":"/ˌɡɪv ˈʌp/","definition":"to stop trying","arabic":"يستسلم","example":"Dana didn't give up.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"Stories about **making a difference** often follow this pattern: a character notices a **problem or an opportunity** → has an **idea** → faces **obstacles** → finds **solutions** with others → creates an **impact** on the community. Tracking this pattern helps you understand both the **plot** and the **theme**.\n\nCharacters **respond** to obstacles in different ways. Notice what the main character **does** when there is a problem (*Instead of giving up, she organized a meeting*). Also watch for **minor characters who change**: Hessa laughs at the beginning but helps and apologizes at the end.\n\nTo explain the **impact**, find **specific details** (*the classrooms under the roof were cooler … the canteen used fresh mint*), not just general words (*it was good*). The **last lines** of a story often reveal the **theme**: *We made it grow together.*","examples":["Opportunity: *flat, empty and burning hot … \"That roof could be a garden.\"*","Obstacle 1 – water: *How will you water the plants?* → Solution: collect the water that drips from the air conditioners.","Obstacle 2 – money: *Who will pay for everything?* → Solution: a fundraising bake sale and a donation of soil.","Obstacle 3 – safety: *How will you keep students safe?* → Solution: visits only with a teacher, behind a new safety railing.","Dana's response: ***Instead of giving up, she organized a meeting.*** → determined, organized.","Hessa's change: *\"Nothing can grow up there.\"* → joins the meeting → *\"I'm sorry I laughed. You were right.\"*","Impact (specific details): *cooler classrooms, fresh mint for the canteen, science lessons among the plants.*","Simile: *the idea stayed in Dana's head like a seed* → the idea grows, like the garden.","Theme: ***\"I only had the idea. We made it grow together.\"*** → one idea + teamwork = real change."],"common_errors":["✗ Thinking Dana did everything alone. → ✓ Many people helped: students, teachers, grandfather, parents, a store. (Teamwork.)","✗ Describing the impact with general words: It was nice. → ✓ Give specific details: cooler classrooms, fresh mint. (Be specific.)","✗ Ignoring minor characters. → ✓ Notice how Hessa changes. (Minor characters can change too.)","✗ Dana give up when the principal asked questions. → ✓ Dana didn't give up; she organized a meeting. (Past simple: **didn't give up**.)","✗ The bake sale raised 2,300 riyals, less than the target. → ✓ It raised 2,300 riyals – 300 more than the target. (Check the numbers.)","✗ The theme is: gardens. → ✓ The theme is: one idea and teamwork can change a community. (A theme is a message.)","✗ Mixing up obstacle and solution. → ✓ Obstacle = the problem; solution = how they fixed it. (Match each pair.)"],"arabic":"قصص صنع الفرق تتبع غالبًا هذا النمط: شخصية تلاحظ مشكلة أو فرصة، ثم تخطر لها فكرة، ثم تواجه عقبات، ثم تجد حلولًا مع الآخرين، ثم تُحدث أثرًا في المجتمع.\n\nلاحظ كيف تستجيب الشخصية للعقبات: «بدل أن تستسلم نظّمت اجتماعًا»، ولاحظ الشخصيات الثانوية التي تتغير، فحصة سخرت في البداية ثم ساعدت واعتذرت في النهاية.\n\nلشرح الأثر اذكر تفاصيل محددة (فصول أبرد، نعناع طازج للمقصف) لا كلمات عامة، والسطور الأخيرة تكشف غالبًا الفكرة العامة: «صنعناها تنمو معًا».\n\nانتبه: give up تعني يستسلم، ونفيها في الماضي didn't give up."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:30","narration":"Flat, empty and burning hot – Dana looked at the school roof and saw… a garden.","on_screen":"The Garden on the Roof 🌿","visual":"A dusty school roof in Riyadh; a girl at a window with a notebook."},{"time":"00:30–01:40","narration":"How will you water the plants? Who will pay? How will you keep students safe?","on_screen":"Three obstacles","visual":"Three question marks appear over the principal's desk."},{"time":"01:40–02:40","narration":"Air-conditioner water, a bake sale, Grandfather's advice, a safety railing…","on_screen":"Solutions – together","visual":"Students collecting AC water, selling cakes, building planters; a railing installed."},{"time":"02:40–03:30","narration":"Cooler classrooms, fresh mint, science lessons among the plants – a bigger difference than anyone expected!","on_screen":"Impact","visual":"The rooftop garden in bloom with bees and students."},{"time":"03:30–04:00","narration":"\"I only had the idea. We made it grow together.\"","on_screen":"Theme","visual":"Dana and Hessa watering basil at sunset."}],"captions_ar":["مستوٍ وفارغ وشديد الحرارة: نظرت دانة إلى سطح المدرسة فرأت… حديقة.","كيف ستسقين النباتات؟ ومن سيدفع؟ وكيف ستحافظين على سلامة الطلاب؟","ماء المكيفات، وبيع الكعك، ونصيحة الجد، ودرابزين للسلامة…","فصول أبرد، ونعناع طازج، ودروس علوم بين النباتات: فرق أكبر مما توقّعه أحد!","«كانت الفكرة فكرتي فقط، لكننا جعلناها تنمو معًا»."],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm female storyteller voice, speed 1.0. Separate voices for Dana, Hessa, Ms. Nouf and Grandfather."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Garden on the Roof","body":"Every morning, Dana climbed the stairs to her Grade 7 classroom and looked out of the window at the same thing: the school roof. It was flat, empty and burning hot, covered in dust and a few broken chairs.\n\n\"What a waste,\" she said one day. \"That roof could be a garden.\"\n\nHer friends laughed. \"A garden? On a roof? In Riyadh?\" said Hessa. \"Nothing can grow up there.\"\n\nBut the idea stayed in Dana's head like a seed. That weekend, she searched online and discovered that rooftop gardens grow in hot cities around the world. Plants on a roof can give shade, cool the building below and even provide fresh herbs. She filled three pages of her notebook with plans.\n\nOn Sunday, she knocked on the principal's door. Ms. Nouf listened carefully, then asked three questions. \"How will you water the plants? Who will pay for everything? And how will you keep students safe on the roof?\"\n\nDana didn't have all the answers yet. Instead of giving up, she organized a meeting. Twelve students came, and even Hessa joined. Dana wrote every idea on the whiteboard, and by the end of the hour, the board was full. Together, they found solutions. The science teacher, Ms. Reem, showed them how to collect the water that drips from the air conditioners. The art club designed posters for a fundraising bake sale. Dana's grandfather, who had been a farmer in Al-Qassim, explained which plants could survive the heat: mint, basil, aloe and small native shrubs.\n\nTwo weeks later, Dana returned to the principal's office with a written plan. It showed a water system made from recycled bottles, a budget, and a promise that students would visit the roof only with a teacher, behind a new safety railing.\n\nMs. Nouf read every page. Then she smiled. \"If the bake sale reaches its target, I will pay for the railing,\" she said.\n\nThe bake sale raised 2,300 riyals – 300 more than the target. A hardware store in the neighborhood donated soil, and parents spent a Saturday morning building wooden planters. By the end of the term, the empty roof had become a green garden full of herbs, flowers and buzzing bees.\n\nThe garden made a bigger difference than anyone had expected. The classrooms under the roof were cooler, the canteen used fresh mint in its lemon drinks, and younger students came up with their teachers for science lessons among the plants. Some families even asked for cuttings to start small gardens on their own roofs.\n\nOn the last day of school, Hessa found Dana watering the basil. \"I'm sorry I laughed,\" she said. \"You were right.\"\n\nDana shook her head. \"I only had the idea,\" she said. \"We made it grow together.\"","word_count":459,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L06-U6-LS2-1","genre":"narrative","role":"main","difficulty":"700L–850L","glossary":[{"word":"budget","definition":"a plan for how much money you will spend","arabic":"ميزانية"},{"word":"railing","definition":"a fence of bars that stops people from falling","arabic":"درابزين"},{"word":"donate","definition":"to give something to help others","arabic":"يتبرع"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the story. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ القصة واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What did Dana see from her classroom window every morning?","answer":"the flat, empty school roof","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"سطح المدرسة الفارغ.","options":["the flat, empty school roof","a park","the school garden","the playground"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Hessa say when she first heard the idea?","answer":"Nothing can grow up there.","explanation":"Paragraph 3.","explanation_ar":"لا شيء ينمو هناك.","options":["What a great idea!","Nothing can grow up there.","Let's start tomorrow.","I'll ask the principal."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Who showed the students how to collect water from the air conditioners?","answer":"Ms. Reem, the science teacher","explanation":"Paragraph 6.","explanation_ar":"المعلمة ريم.","options":["Ms. Nouf, the principal","Dana's grandfather","Ms. Reem, the science teacher","Hessa"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which plants did Dana's grandfather suggest?","answer":"mint, basil, aloe and small native shrubs","explanation":"Paragraph 6.","explanation_ar":"النعناع والريحان والصبار والشجيرات المحلية.","options":["roses and tulips","mint, basil, aloe and small native shrubs","apple and orange trees","rice and wheat"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How much did the bake sale raise?","answer":"2,300 riyals","explanation":"Paragraph 9.","explanation_ar":"2300 ريال.","options":["2,300 riyals","2,000 riyals","300 riyals","3,200 riyals"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did the hardware store donate?","answer":"soil","explanation":"Paragraph 9.","explanation_ar":"التربة.","options":["a railing","wooden planters","seeds","soil"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS2-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Obstacles, solutions and change. Choose.","instructions_ar":"العقبات والحلول والتغيّر: اختر.","items":[{"q":"How did the students solve the WATER problem?","answer":"They collected the water that drips from the air conditioners.","explanation":"Obstacle → solution.","explanation_ar":"جمعوا ماء المكيفات.","options":["They bought bottled water.","They collected the water that drips from the air conditioners.","They waited for rain.","They used water from the canteen."],"dok":2,"skill":"problem and solution","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What did Dana do when she didn't have all the answers?","answer":"She organized a meeting to find solutions with others.","explanation":"Character response.","explanation_ar":"نظّمت اجتماعًا.","options":["She gave up on the idea.","She organized a meeting to find solutions with others.","She asked Hessa to stop laughing.","She built the garden alone."],"dok":2,"skill":"character","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What does the simile *the idea stayed in Dana's head like a seed* suggest?","answer":"The idea would grow, just like a plant.","explanation":"Figurative language.","explanation_ar":"الفكرة ستنمو.","options":["Dana had a headache.","Dana was thinking about food.","The idea would grow, just like a plant.","The idea was very small and unimportant."],"dok":2,"skill":"figurative language","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How does Hessa CHANGE during the rooftop-garden story?","answer":"She goes from laughing at the idea to helping and apologizing.","explanation":"Character change.","explanation_ar":"من السخرية إلى المساعدة والاعتذار.","options":["She goes from laughing at the idea to helping and apologizing.","She goes from helping to laughing.","She becomes the principal.","She doesn't change at all."],"dok":2,"skill":"character change","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why did Ms. Nouf agree to pay for the railing?","answer":"Dana's plan answered her questions about water, money and safety.","explanation":"Inference.","explanation_ar":"لأن الخطة أجابت عن أسئلتها.","options":["Hessa asked her to.","The railing was free.","She wanted a new office.","Dana's plan answered her questions about water, money and safety."],"dok":3,"skill":"inference","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which detail shows the impact on YOUNGER students?","answer":"They came up with their teachers for science lessons among the plants.","explanation":"Impact.","explanation_ar":"دروس العلوم بين النباتات.","options":["They came up with their teachers for science lessons among the plants.","The canteen used fresh mint.","The classrooms were cooler.","Parents built planters."],"dok":2,"skill":"key details","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS2-A3","type":"highlight","stage":"freer","instructions":"Find the evidence: Find the evidence.","instructions_ar":"ابحث عن الدليل.","items":[{"q":"Underline the sentence that shows Dana's response to an obstacle.","answer":"Instead of giving up, she organized a meeting.","explanation":"Character response.","explanation_ar":"استجابة الشخصية.","evidence":"Instead of giving up, she organized a meeting.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L06-U6-LS2-1","dok":2,"skill":"character","stage":"freer","sentences":["Every morning, Dana climbed the stairs to her Grade 7 classroom and looked out of the window at the same thing: the school roof.","It was flat, empty and burning hot, covered in dust and a few broken chairs.","\"What a waste,\" she said one day.","\"That roof could be a garden.\"","Her friends laughed.","\"A garden?","On a roof?","In Riyadh?\" said Hessa.","\"Nothing can grow up there.\"","But the idea stayed in Dana's head like a seed.","That weekend, she searched online and discovered that rooftop gardens grow in hot cities around the world.","Plants on a roof can give shade, cool the building below and even provide fresh herbs.","She filled three pages of her notebook with plans.","On Sunday, she knocked on the principal's door.","Ms.","Nouf listened carefully, then asked three questions.","\"How will you water the plants?","Who will pay for everything?","And how will you keep students safe on the roof?\"","Dana didn't have all the answers yet.","Instead of giving up, she organized a meeting.","Twelve students came, and even Hessa joined.","Dana wrote every idea on the whiteboard, and by the end of the hour, the board was full.","Together, they found solutions.","The science teacher, Ms.","Reem, showed them how to collect the water that drips from the air conditioners.","The art club designed posters for a fundraising bake sale.","Dana's grandfather, who had been a farmer in Al-Qassim, explained which plants could survive the heat: mint, basil, aloe and small native shrubs.","Two weeks later, Dana returned to the principal's office with a written plan.","It showed a water system made from recycled bottles, a budget, and a promise that students would visit the roof only with a teacher, behind a new safety railing.","Ms.","Nouf read every page.","Then she smiled.","\"If the bake sale reaches its target, I will pay for the railing,\" she said.","The bake sale raised 2,300 riyals – 300 more than the target.","A hardware store in the neighborhood donated soil, and parents spent a Saturday morning building wooden planters.","By the end of the term, the empty roof had become a green garden full of herbs, flowers and buzzing bees.","The garden made a bigger difference than anyone had expected.","The classrooms under the roof were cooler, the canteen used fresh mint in its lemon drinks, and younger students came up with their teachers for science lessons among the plants.","Some families even asked for cuttings to start small gardens on their own roofs.","On the last day of school, Hessa found Dana watering the basil.","\"I'm sorry I laughed,\" she said.","\"You were right.\"","Dana shook her head.","\"I only had the idea,\" she said.","\"We made it grow together.\""]},{"q":"Underline the sentence that states the theme.","answer":"\"I only had the idea,\" she said. \"We made it grow together.\"","explanation":"Theme.","explanation_ar":"الفكرة العامة.","evidence":"\"I only had the idea,\" she said. \"We made it grow together.\"","text_id":"TXT-RW-L06-U6-LS2-1","dok":3,"skill":"theme","stage":"freer","sentences":["Every morning, Dana climbed the stairs to her Grade 7 classroom and looked out of the window at the same thing: the school roof.","It was flat, empty and burning hot, covered in dust and a few broken chairs.","\"What a waste,\" she said one day.","\"That roof could be a garden.\"","Her friends laughed.","\"A garden?","On a roof?","In Riyadh?\" said Hessa.","\"Nothing can grow up there.\"","But the idea stayed in Dana's head like a seed.","That weekend, she searched online and discovered that rooftop gardens grow in hot cities around the world.","Plants on a roof can give shade, cool the building below and even provide fresh herbs.","She filled three pages of her notebook with plans.","On Sunday, she knocked on the principal's door.","Ms.","Nouf listened carefully, then asked three questions.","\"How will you water the plants?","Who will pay for everything?","And how will you keep students safe on the roof?\"","Dana didn't have all the answers yet.","Instead of giving up, she organized a meeting.","Twelve students came, and even Hessa joined.","Dana wrote every idea on the whiteboard, and by the end of the hour, the board was full.","Together, they found solutions.","The science teacher, Ms.","Reem, showed them how to collect the water that drips from the air conditioners.","The art club designed posters for a fundraising bake sale.","Dana's grandfather, who had been a farmer in Al-Qassim, explained which plants could survive the heat: mint, basil, aloe and small native shrubs.","Two weeks later, Dana returned to the principal's office with a written plan.","It showed a water system made from recycled bottles, a budget, and a promise that students would visit the roof only with a teacher, behind a new safety railing.","Ms.","Nouf read every page.","Then she smiled.","\"If the bake sale reaches its target, I will pay for the railing,\" she said.","The bake sale raised 2,300 riyals – 300 more than the target.","A hardware store in the neighborhood donated soil, and parents spent a Saturday morning building wooden planters.","By the end of the term, the empty roof had become a green garden full of herbs, flowers and buzzing bees.","The garden made a bigger difference than anyone had expected.","The classrooms under the roof were cooler, the canteen used fresh mint in its lemon drinks, and younger students came up with their teachers for science lessons among the plants.","Some families even asked for cuttings to start small gardens on their own roofs.","On the last day of school, Hessa found Dana watering the basil.","\"I'm sorry I laughed,\" she said.","\"You were right.\"","Dana shook her head.","\"I only had the idea,\" she said.","\"We made it grow together.\""]},{"q":"Why does the author include the principal's three questions?","answer":"to show realistic obstacles that Dana must solve before the idea can happen","explanation":"Author's craft.","explanation_ar":"لإظهار عقبات واقعية.","options":["to make Ms. Nouf look unkind","to end the story quickly","to show realistic obstacles that Dana must solve before the idea can happen","to describe the weather"],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft","stage":"freer"},{"q":"What does *The garden made a bigger difference than anyone had expected* tell the reader?","answer":"The project's impact went beyond growing plants.","explanation":"Inference.","explanation_ar":"الأثر تجاوز الزراعة.","options":["The garden was very large.","The garden failed.","Nobody liked the garden.","The project's impact went beyond growing plants."],"dok":2,"skill":"inference","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS2-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Explain the story.","instructions_ar":"اشرح القصة.","items":[{"q":"List the three obstacles and their solutions.","answer":"Water → collect AC water with a bottle system. Money → bake sale (2,300 riyals) and donated soil. Safety → visits only with a teacher behind a new railing.","explanation":"Obstacles.","explanation_ar":"العقبات.","dok":2,"skill":"problem and solution","stage":"production"},{"q":"Name two traits of Dana and give evidence for each.","answer":"Determined: she didn't give up after the principal's questions. Organized: she wrote a plan with a water system, a budget and safety rules.","explanation":"Traits.","explanation_ar":"الصفات.","dok":2,"skill":"character traits","stage":"production"},{"q":"Explain the impact of the garden with three specific details.","answer":"The classrooms under the roof became cooler, the canteen used fresh mint in its drinks, and younger students had science lessons among the plants.","explanation":"Impact.","explanation_ar":"الأثر.","dok":2,"skill":"key details","stage":"production"},{"q":"What is the theme of the story? Use the last line as evidence.","answer":"One idea can change a community when people work together; Dana says, 'I only had the idea. We made it grow together.'","explanation":"Theme.","explanation_ar":"الفكرة العامة.","dok":3,"skill":"theme","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS2-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"The Garden on the Roof\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “The Garden on the Roof”.","answer":"459 words","title":"The Garden on the Roof","body":"Every morning, Dana climbed the stairs to her Grade 7 classroom and looked out of the window at the same thing: the school roof. It was flat, empty and burning hot, covered in dust and a few broken chairs.\n\n\"What a waste,\" she said one day. \"That roof could be a garden.\"\n\nHer friends laughed. \"A garden? On a roof? In Riyadh?\" said Hessa. \"Nothing can grow up there.\"\n\nBut the idea stayed in Dana's head like a seed. That weekend, she searched online and discovered that rooftop gardens grow in hot cities around the world. Plants on a roof can give shade, cool the building below and even provide fresh herbs. She filled three pages of her notebook with plans.\n\nOn Sunday, she knocked on the principal's door. Ms. Nouf listened carefully, then asked three questions. \"How will you water the plants? Who will pay for everything? And how will you keep students safe on the roof?\"\n\nDana didn't have all the answers yet. Instead of giving up, she organized a meeting. Twelve students came, and even Hessa joined. Dana wrote every idea on the whiteboard, and by the end of the hour, the board was full. Together, they found solutions. The science teacher, Ms. Reem, showed them how to collect the water that drips from the air conditioners. The art club designed posters for a fundraising bake sale. Dana's grandfather, who had been a farmer in Al-Qassim, explained which plants could survive the heat: mint, basil, aloe and small native shrubs.\n\nTwo weeks later, Dana returned to the principal's office with a written plan. It showed a water system made from recycled bottles, a budget, and a promise that students would visit the roof only with a teacher, behind a new safety railing.\n\nMs. Nouf read every page. Then she smiled. \"If the bake sale reaches its target, I will pay for the railing,\" she said.\n\nThe bake sale raised 2,300 riyals – 300 more than the target. A hardware store in the neighborhood donated soil, and parents spent a Saturday morning building wooden planters. By the end of the term, the empty roof had become a green garden full of herbs, flowers and buzzing bees.\n\nThe garden made a bigger difference than anyone had expected. The classrooms under the roof were cooler, the canteen used fresh mint in its lemon drinks, and younger students came up with their teachers for science lessons among the plants. Some families even asked for cuttings to start small gardens on their own roofs.\n\nOn the last day of school, Hessa found Dana watering the basil. \"I'm sorry I laughed,\" she said. \"You were right.\"\n\nDana shook her head. \"I only had the idea,\" she said. \"We made it grow together.\"","words":459,"limit":254}],"time_limit_sec":254},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS2-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Change Map","instructions":"Organizer: Track the problem, the obstacles and solutions, the character changes and the impact.","items":[{"q":"Opportunity and idea","answer":"An empty, hot roof → Dana's idea: a rooftop garden."},{"q":"Obstacle 1 + solution (water)","answer":"How to water the plants? → collect the water that drips from the air conditioners; a system of recycled bottles."},{"q":"Obstacle 2 + solution (money)","answer":"Who will pay? → a bake sale that raised 2,300 riyals; a store donated soil; parents built planters."},{"q":"Obstacle 3 + solution (safety)","answer":"How to keep students safe? → visits only with a teacher, behind a new safety railing paid for by the principal."},{"q":"How Dana and Hessa change","answer":"Dana: from an idea to a leader who organizes others. Hessa: from laughing to helping and apologizing."},{"q":"Impact and theme","answer":"cooler classrooms, fresh mint, science lessons; theme: one idea and teamwork can change a community."}]}],"game":{"name":"Obstacle Course","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Garden builder: the child faces an obstacle on the roof and chooses the best solution from three; each correct choice adds a plant to the rooftop garden. A complete garden shows the impact on the school.","Teams move along the path from IDEA to IMPACT.","On each obstacle space, they draw an obstacle card and must find the matching solution card.","They explain the solution using evidence from the story.","A wrong match means they miss a turn.","Correct match = move 2 spaces; first team to IMPACT wins."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is an *obstacle*?","answer":"something that makes it hard to do what you want","explanation":"Vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"عقبة.","options":["a kind of plant","a school roof","something that makes it hard to do what you want","a fundraiser"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"In Dana's plan, what is a *budget*?","answer":"a plan for how much money you will spend","explanation":"Vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"ميزانية.","options":["a garden tool","a kind of herb","a plan for how much money you will spend","a safety rule"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*A store **donated** soil for the garden.* *Donated* means ___.","answer":"gave to help","explanation":"Context.","explanation_ar":"تبرّع.","options":["sold","carried","watered","gave to help"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Who was Ms. Nouf?","answer":"the principal","explanation":"Key detail.","explanation_ar":"المديرة.","options":["the science teacher","Dana's grandmother","the art club leader","the principal"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details"},{"q":"Which sentence about Dana is correct?","answer":"Dana didn't give up when she faced obstacles.","explanation":"Past simple negative.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Dana didn't give up when she faced obstacles.","Dana didn't gave up when she faced obstacles.","Dana don't give up when she faced obstacles.","Dana not give up when she faced obstacles."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Why did Dana's friends laugh at first?","answer":"They didn't believe anything could grow on a hot roof in Riyadh.","explanation":"Inference.","explanation_ar":"لم يصدقوا أن شيئًا ينمو.","options":["Dana told a joke.","They didn't believe anything could grow on a hot roof in Riyadh.","The principal was funny.","The roof was full of plants."],"dok":2,"skill":"inference"},{"q":"Which detail BEST shows that the community helped?","answer":"A hardware store donated soil, and parents built wooden planters.","explanation":"Evidence.","explanation_ar":"تبرع المتجر وبناء الآباء.","options":["A hardware store donated soil, and parents built wooden planters.","Dana looked out of the window.","Hessa laughed.","The roof was hot."],"dok":2,"skill":"claims and evidence"},{"q":"Which trait does Dana show when she writes a plan with a budget and safety rules?","answer":"organized","explanation":"Trait.","explanation_ar":"منظّمة.","options":["careless","shy","lazy","organized"],"dok":2,"skill":"character traits"},{"q":"Why does Dana say *We made it grow together*?","answer":"She wants to show that the success belonged to everyone who helped.","explanation":"Inference.","explanation_ar":"النجاح للجميع.","options":["She is angry with Hessa.","She wants a prize.","She wants to show that the success belonged to everyone who helped.","She didn't like the garden."],"dok":3,"skill":"inference"},{"q":"Which statement BEST expresses the theme of *The Garden on the Roof*?","answer":"One good idea can change a community when people work together.","explanation":"Theme.","explanation_ar":"فكرة واحدة مع التعاون تغيّر المجتمع.","options":["Roofs should always stay empty.","One good idea can change a community when people work together.","Bake sales are better than gardens.","Principals never say yes."],"dok":3,"skill":"theme"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'obstacle': a rock blocking a path"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'budget': a notebook with prices and a total"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'railing': a metal railing on a roof"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'donate': a store owner giving bags of soil"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'planter': wooden boxes full of plants"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'herb': mint and basil in pots"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'give up': a student continuing to climb a steep path"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-01","prompt":"An empty school roof seen from a classroom window."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-02","prompt":"Students, teachers and parents solving problems together."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS2-03","prompt":"The rooftop garden in bloom."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V01","script":"obstacle. Water was the biggest obstacle."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V02","script":"budget. Dana's plan included a budget."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V03","script":"railing. A new safety railing was built on the roof."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V04","script":"donate. A store donated soil for the garden."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V05","script":"planter. Parents built wooden planters."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V06","script":"herb. The garden grew fresh herbs."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-V07","script":"give up. Dana didn't give up."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-T1","script":"Every morning, Dana climbed the stairs to her Grade 7 classroom and looked out of the window at the same thing: the school roof. It was flat, empty and burning hot, covered in dust and a few broken chairs. \"What a waste,\" she said one day. \"That roof could be a garden.\" Her friends laughed. \"A garden? On a roof? In Riyadh?\" said Hessa. \"Nothing can grow up there.\" But the idea stayed in Dana's head like a seed. That weekend, she searched online and discovered that rooftop gardens grow in hot cities around the world. Plants on a roof can give shade, cool the building below and even provide fresh herbs. She filled three pages of her notebook with plans. On Sunday, she knocked on the principal's door. Ms. Nouf listened carefully, then asked three questions. \"How will you water the plants? Who will pay for everything? And how will you keep students safe on the roof?\" Dana didn't have all the answers yet. Instead of giving up, she organized a meeting. Twelve students came, and even Hessa joined. Dana wrote every idea on the whiteboard, and by the end of the hour, the board was full. Together, they found solutions. The science teacher, Ms. Reem, showed them how to collect the water that drips from the air conditioners. The art club designed posters for a fundraising bake sale. Dana's grandfather, who had been a farmer in Al-Qassim, explained which plants could survive the heat: mint, basil, aloe and small native shrubs. Two weeks later, Dana returned to the principal's office with a written plan. It showed a water system made from recycled bottles, a budget, and a promise that students would visit the roof only with a teacher, behind a new safety railing. Ms. Nouf read every page. Then she smiled. \"If the bake sale reaches its target, I will pay for the railing,\" she said. The bake sale raised 2,300 riyals – 300 more than the target. A hardware store in the neighborhood donated soil, and parents spent a Saturday morning building wooden planters. By the end of the term, the empty roof had become a green garden full of herbs, flowers and buzzing bees. The garden made a bigger difference than anyone had expected. The classrooms under the roof were cooler, the canteen used fresh mint in its lemon drinks, and younger students came up with their teachers for science lessons among the plants. Some families even asked for cuttings to start small gardens on their own roofs. On the last day of school, Hessa found Dana watering the basil. \"I'm sorry I laughed,\" she said. \"You were right.\" Dana shook her head. \"I only had the idea,\" she said. \"We made it grow together.\""},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Flat, empty and burning hot – Dana looked at the school roof and saw… a garden. How will you water the plants? Who will pay? How will you keep students safe? Air-conditioner water, a bake sale, Grandfather's advice, a safety railing… Cooler classrooms, fresh mint, science lessons among the plants – a bigger difference than anyone expected! \"I only had the idea. We made it grow together.\""}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS3","title":"Theme across two texts: \"A Letter to the School Council\"","lesson_type":"strategy_paired_text","objectives":["identify the theme of a story and the message of a formal letter, with evidence","compare a shared theme across two texts of different genres","explain how each genre develops the theme in a different way"],"objectives_ar":["تحديد الفكرة العامة لقصة ورسالة رسالة رسمية بالأدلة.","مقارنة فكرة عامة مشتركة في نصين من نوعين مختلفين.","شرح كيف يطوّر كل نوع أدبي الفكرة العامة بطريقة مختلفة."],"success_criteria":["I can state the theme of each text as a full sentence and support it with evidence.","I can write one shared theme for both texts.","I can explain how the story SHOWS the theme and the letter STATES it."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع صياغة الفكرة العامة لكل نص في جملة كاملة ودعمها بالدليل.","أستطيع كتابة فكرة عامة مشتركة بين النصين.","أستطيع شرح كيف تُظهر القصة الفكرة وكيف تصرّح بها الرسالة."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"program","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈproʊˌɡræm/","definition":"a planned series of activities with a purpose","arabic":"برنامج","example":"Reading Buddies is a new school program.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"supervise","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈsupərˌvaɪz/","definition":"to watch over people to make sure they are safe and doing things correctly","arabic":"يشرف على","example":"Ms. Lama will supervise the program.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"volunteer","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/ˌvɑlənˈtɪr/","definition":"to offer to do something without being paid; a person who does this","arabic":"يتطوع / متطوع","example":"Twenty-four students volunteered.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"proposal","pos":"noun","ipa":"/prəˈpoʊzəl/","definition":"a plan that you suggest for others to consider","arabic":"مقترح","example":"Thank you for considering our proposal.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"grateful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɡreɪtfəl/","definition":"feeling or showing thanks","arabic":"ممتن","example":"I would be grateful for your help.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"patience","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpeɪʃəns/","definition":"the ability to wait or keep trying calmly","arabic":"صبر","example":"Reading with younger children takes patience.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"message","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɛsɪdʒ/","definition":"the main idea or lesson that a writer wants to share","arabic":"رسالة (فكرة يريد الكاتب إيصالها)","example":"The letter's message is that students can help each other.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **theme** is a **message about life** that a text shares. It is written as a **full sentence**, not one word: not *helping*, but ***Young people can make a difference when they work together.*** Different texts – even different **genres** – can share a **similar theme**.\n\nGenres develop themes **differently**. A **story** usually **shows** the theme through **events, characters' changes and dialogue** – you must **infer** it (*\"We made it grow together.\"*). A **formal letter** or an informational text usually **states** its message more **directly** through **reasons and benefits** (*Reading Buddies would benefit both groups*).\n\nTo compare themes: (1) find the **topic** of each text; (2) write the **theme or message** of each with **evidence**; (3) find what is **shared**; (4) explain **how each genre** develops it. Use comparison language: *Both texts show… However, the story… while the letter…*","examples":["Story topic: a rooftop garden. → Theme: ***One idea can change a community when people work together.***","Story evidence: *\"I only had the idea … We made it grow together.\"*","Letter topic: a Reading Buddies program. → Message: ***Students can help each other and their school by planning a useful project.***","Letter evidence: *Reading Buddies would benefit both groups.*","Shared theme: ***Young people can make a difference by noticing a need, planning carefully and working with others.***","Both noticed a need: Dana – an empty roof; Yara – younger students who find long words difficult.","Both planned carefully: Dana – a budget and safety rules; Yara – times, teacher supervision and a review in January.","Story SHOWS: Hessa's change and Dana's actions. Letter STATES: *The younger students would get extra reading practice.*","Comparison sentence: ***Both texts show that young people can improve their school; however, the story shows it through events, while the letter explains it with reasons.***"],"common_errors":["✗ Writing the theme as one word: teamwork. → ✓ Write a full sentence: Teamwork can turn an idea into reality. (Theme = sentence.)","✗ Confusing topic and theme. → ✓ Topic: a garden. Theme: the lesson about life. (Topic ≠ theme.)","✗ A theme with no evidence. → ✓ Quote or paraphrase a line from each text. (Support it.)","✗ Saying the texts are the same. → ✓ Explain how each genre develops the theme differently. (Same theme, different ways.)","✗ Both text shows the theme. → ✓ Both texts show the theme. (both + plural noun + plural verb.)","✗ The letter shows the theme through dialogue. → ✓ The letter states its message through reasons and benefits. (Know the genre.)","✗ Choosing a theme that fits only one text. → ✓ Check that the shared theme fits BOTH texts. (Test it on both.)"],"arabic":"الفكرة العامة رسالة عن الحياة يقدّمها النص، وتُكتب في جملة كاملة لا في كلمة واحدة، وقد تشترك نصوص مختلفة، حتى من أنواع أدبية مختلفة، في فكرة متقاربة.\n\nتطوّر الأنواع الأدبية الفكرة بطرق مختلفة: القصة تُظهرها من خلال الأحداث وتغيّر الشخصيات والحوار فنستنتجها، أما الرسالة الرسمية فتصرّح برسالتها مباشرة من خلال الأسباب والفوائد.\n\nللمقارنة: حدّد موضوع كل نص، ثم فكرته بالدليل، ثم ما يشتركان فيه، ثم كيف يطوّر كل نوع الفكرة. واستخدم: Both texts show… However, the story… while the letter…\n\nانتبه: الموضوع (حديقة) غير الفكرة العامة (فكرة واحدة مع التعاون تغيّر المجتمع)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:30","narration":"A garden on a roof. Reading buddies in the classroom. Two different texts – one big idea?","on_screen":"Theme Across Two Texts 📖✉️","visual":"A rooftop garden and a Grade 7 student reading with a Grade 3 child."},{"time":"00:30–01:40","narration":"Dear Members of the School Council, I am writing to request your approval for a new program called Reading Buddies…","on_screen":"(the letter)","visual":"Yara writing at a desk; then older students reading with younger ones."},{"time":"01:40–02:40","narration":"The story SHOWS its theme through events and characters. The letter STATES its message through reasons.","on_screen":"Shows ↔ States","visual":"Split screen: Dana watering basil / a letter's 'benefits' paragraph highlighted."},{"time":"02:40–03:30","narration":"Both texts: notice a need → plan carefully → work with others → make a difference!","on_screen":"Shared theme","visual":"Two paths join into one road labeled MAKING A DIFFERENCE."},{"time":"03:30–04:00","narration":"Write the theme as a sentence, support it with evidence – and compare!","on_screen":"Theme = sentence + evidence","visual":"A theme sentence appears with two evidence cards beneath it."}],"captions_ar":["حديقة على السطح، ورفاق قراءة في الصف. نصان مختلفان وفكرة كبيرة واحدة؟","أعضاء مجلس المدرسة الكرام، أكتب إليكم لأطلب موافقتكم على برنامج جديد اسمه رفاق القراءة…","القصة تُظهر فكرتها من خلال الأحداث والشخصيات، والرسالة تصرّح برسالتها من خلال الأسباب.","في النصين: ملاحظة حاجة ← تخطيط دقيق ← عمل مع الآخرين ← إحداث فرق!","اكتب الفكرة العامة في جملة، وادعمها بالدليل، ثم قارن!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, clear female voice, speed 1.0. Yara reads her letter."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"A Letter to the School Council","body":"**To:** The School Council, Al-Noor Intermediate School · **From:** Yara Al-Harbi, Class Representative, Grade 7B · **Date:** October 10 · **Subject:** Request to start a Reading Buddies program\n\nDear Members of the School Council,\n\nI am writing to request your approval for a new program called Reading Buddies. In this program, students from Grade 7 would read with students from Grade 3 for twenty minutes, twice a week, during the morning activity period.\n\nLast month, our class visited the Grade 3 classrooms and listened to the children read. We noticed that many of them enjoy stories but still find long words difficult. At the same time, several of my classmates told me that they wanted to do something useful for our school community.\n\nReading Buddies would benefit both groups. The younger students would get extra reading practice and a friendly older student to encourage them. The older students would develop patience, leadership and communication skills. In addition, the program would cost almost nothing, because we would use books from the school library.\n\nSo far, twenty-four students from Grade 7 have volunteered to participate, and Ms. Lama, our English teacher, has kindly agreed to supervise the program. We would like to start in November and review our progress in January.\n\nI would be grateful if the council could approve this request at its next meeting. I would also be happy to present our plan in person and answer any questions. Thank you very much for taking the time to consider our proposal.\n\nSincerely,\n\nYara Al-Harbi\n\nClass Representative, Grade 7B","word_count":255,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L06-U6-LS3-1","genre":"letter/email","role":"paired","difficulty":"700L–850L","glossary":[{"word":"council","definition":"a group of people who meet to make decisions","arabic":"مجلس"},{"word":"supervise","definition":"to watch over people to make sure they are safe and doing things correctly","arabic":"يشرف على"},{"word":"proposal","definition":"a plan that you suggest for others to consider","arabic":"مقترح"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the letter. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ الرسالة واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"Who wrote *A Letter to the School Council*?","answer":"Yara Al-Harbi, class representative of Grade 7B","explanation":"Header.","explanation_ar":"يارا الحربي.","options":["Ms. Lama, the English teacher","Dana, the garden leader","the school council","Yara Al-Harbi, class representative of Grade 7B"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What does Yara request?","answer":"approval for a Reading Buddies program","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"الموافقة على برنامج رفاق القراءة.","options":["approval for a Reading Buddies program","money for a rooftop garden","a new library building","a longer morning break"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How often would the buddies read together?","answer":"for twenty minutes, twice a week","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"عشرون دقيقة مرتين أسبوعيًا.","options":["for one hour every day","once a month","for twenty minutes, twice a week","only on weekends"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did the class notice when they visited Grade 3?","answer":"Many children enjoy stories but find long words difficult.","explanation":"Paragraph 2.","explanation_ar":"يحبون القصص وتصعب عليهم الكلمات الطويلة.","options":["The children did not like stories.","Many children enjoy stories but find long words difficult.","The children read better than Grade 7.","There were no books in Grade 3."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Who agreed to supervise the program?","answer":"Ms. Lama, the English teacher","explanation":"Paragraph 4.","explanation_ar":"المعلمة لمى.","options":["Ms. Lama, the English teacher","the principal","the parents","Yara herself"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why would the program cost almost nothing?","answer":"They would use books from the school library.","explanation":"Paragraph 3.","explanation_ar":"سيستخدمون كتب المكتبة.","options":["Parents would pay for it.","They would use books from the school library.","The council would buy new books.","They would sell cakes."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS3-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Theme across texts. Choose.","instructions_ar":"الفكرة العامة عبر النصين: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which is the TOPIC of Yara's letter (not the theme)?","answer":"a Reading Buddies program","explanation":"Topic vs. theme.","explanation_ar":"الموضوع.","options":["Students can help each other and their school.","a Reading Buddies program","Young people can make a difference.","Careful planning leads to success."],"dok":1,"skill":"theme","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which is the BEST statement of the story's theme?","answer":"One idea can change a community when people work together.","explanation":"Theme.","explanation_ar":"أفضل صياغة.","options":["One idea can change a community when people work together.","gardens","Roofs are hot in Riyadh.","Bake sales raise money."],"dok":2,"skill":"theme","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence from the letter BEST supports its message that both groups would gain?","answer":"Reading Buddies would benefit both groups.","explanation":"Evidence.","explanation_ar":"الدليل الأقوى.","options":["Dear Members of the School Council,","We would like to start in November.","Sincerely,","Reading Buddies would benefit both groups."],"dok":2,"skill":"supporting evidence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which SHARED theme fits both *The Garden on the Roof* and Yara's letter?","answer":"Young people can make a difference by noticing a need, planning carefully and working with others.","explanation":"Shared theme.","explanation_ar":"الفكرة المشتركة.","options":["Gardens are better than libraries.","Principals always say yes.","Older students should read alone.","Young people can make a difference by noticing a need, planning carefully and working with others."],"dok":2,"skill":"theme","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How does the STORY develop its theme differently from the letter?","answer":"It shows the theme through events and characters' changes instead of stating it directly.","explanation":"Genre.","explanation_ar":"تُظهره بالأحداث والشخصيات.","options":["It lists benefits in numbered points.","It uses a formal greeting.","It shows the theme through events and characters' changes instead of stating it directly.","It asks the council for approval."],"dok":3,"skill":"comparing texts","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How are Dana and Yara ALIKE?","answer":"Both noticed a need and planned carefully before asking for approval.","explanation":"Compare characters.","explanation_ar":"كلتاهما لاحظت حاجة وخططت.","options":["Both built a garden.","Both wrote to the council.","Both noticed a need and planned carefully before asking for approval.","Both are teachers."],"dok":3,"skill":"comparing texts","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS3-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Complete the Theme Across Texts chart.","instructions_ar":"أكمل جدول الفكرة العامة عبر النصين.","items":[{"q":"Write the topic and the theme of the story, with evidence.","answer":"Topic: a student turns an empty roof into a garden. Theme: one idea can change a community when people work together. Evidence: \"We made it grow together.\"","explanation":"Story.","explanation_ar":"القصة.","dok":2,"skill":"theme","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Write the topic and the message of the letter, with evidence.","answer":"Topic: a Reading Buddies program. Message: students can help each other with a well-planned project. Evidence: \"Reading Buddies would benefit both groups.\"","explanation":"Letter.","explanation_ar":"الرسالة.","dok":2,"skill":"theme","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Write one shared theme for both texts as a full sentence.","answer":"Young people can make a difference by noticing a need, planning carefully and working with others.","explanation":"Shared theme.","explanation_ar":"الفكرة المشتركة.","dok":3,"skill":"theme","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Explain how the story SHOWS the theme and the letter STATES it.","answer":"The story shows the theme through Dana's actions, Hessa's change and the final dialogue, while the letter states its message directly with reasons, benefits and a request.","explanation":"Genre.","explanation_ar":"النوع.","dok":3,"skill":"comparing texts","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS3-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Compare and connect.","instructions_ar":"قارن واربط.","items":[{"q":"Write a comparison sentence using *Both texts… However, … while …*","answer":"Both texts show that young people can improve their school; however, the story shows it through events, while the letter explains it with reasons.","explanation":"Compare.","explanation_ar":"قارن.","dok":3,"skill":"comparing texts","stage":"production"},{"q":"Find one formal phrase in Yara's letter and explain why it fits a letter to the council.","answer":"\"I would be grateful if the council could approve this request\" – it is polite and formal, which shows respect for the council.","explanation":"Formal language.","explanation_ar":"لغة رسمية.","dok":2,"skill":"formal language","stage":"production"},{"q":"How might Hessa from the story react to Yara's Reading Buddies idea? Explain.","answer":"After the garden, Hessa would probably support it and volunteer, because she learned that good ideas can work when people help.","explanation":"Inference.","explanation_ar":"استنتاج.","dok":3,"skill":"inference","stage":"production"},{"q":"What need do you notice at your school, and how could students help?","answer":"Many students forget their water bottles, so we could start a refill station and remind classmates to bring reusable bottles.","explanation":"Connect.","explanation_ar":"ربط.","dok":2,"skill":"connect","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS3-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"A Letter to the School Council\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “A Letter to the School Council”.","answer":"255 words","title":"A Letter to the School Council","body":"**To:** The School Council, Al-Noor Intermediate School · **From:** Yara Al-Harbi, Class Representative, Grade 7B · **Date:** October 10 · **Subject:** Request to start a Reading Buddies program\n\nDear Members of the School Council,\n\nI am writing to request your approval for a new program called Reading Buddies. In this program, students from Grade 7 would read with students from Grade 3 for twenty minutes, twice a week, during the morning activity period.\n\nLast month, our class visited the Grade 3 classrooms and listened to the children read. We noticed that many of them enjoy stories but still find long words difficult. At the same time, several of my classmates told me that they wanted to do something useful for our school community.\n\nReading Buddies would benefit both groups. The younger students would get extra reading practice and a friendly older student to encourage them. The older students would develop patience, leadership and communication skills. In addition, the program would cost almost nothing, because we would use books from the school library.\n\nSo far, twenty-four students from Grade 7 have volunteered to participate, and Ms. Lama, our English teacher, has kindly agreed to supervise the program. We would like to start in November and review our progress in January.\n\nI would be grateful if the council could approve this request at its next meeting. I would also be happy to present our plan in person and answer any questions. Thank you very much for taking the time to consider our proposal.\n\nSincerely,\n\nYara Al-Harbi\n\nClass Representative, Grade 7B","words":255,"limit":148}],"time_limit_sec":148},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS3-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Theme Across Texts","instructions":"Organizer: Write the topic and theme of each text with evidence, then the shared theme and how each genre shows it.","items":[{"q":"Story – topic","answer":"a student turns an empty school roof into a garden"},{"q":"Story – theme + evidence","answer":"One idea can change a community when people work together. – \"We made it grow together.\""},{"q":"Letter – topic","answer":"a request to start a Reading Buddies program"},{"q":"Letter – message + evidence","answer":"Students can help each other and their school with a well-planned project. – \"Reading Buddies would benefit both groups.\""},{"q":"Shared theme (one sentence)","answer":"Young people can make a difference by noticing a need, planning carefully and working with others."},{"q":"How the story SHOWS it and the letter STATES it","answer":"The story shows it through Dana's actions and Hessa's change; the letter states it through clear reasons, benefits and a polite request."}]}],"game":{"name":"Theme Bridge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Bridge builder: the child chooses a shared theme, then drags evidence from each text onto bridge planks. Evidence that doesn't support the theme makes a plank fall. A complete bridge lets Dana and Yara meet in the middle.","Each team chooses one theme-sentence card.","They test it: does it fit BOTH texts?","If yes, they find two pieces of evidence from each text and place them as planks.","They explain how each genre shows the theme.","Shared theme = 2 points; each correct plank = 1 point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is a *theme*?","answer":"a message about life that a text shares","explanation":"Definition.","explanation_ar":"الفكرة العامة.","options":["the title of a text","the place where a story happens","a message about life that a text shares","a list of characters"],"dok":1,"skill":"theme"},{"q":"What does *supervise* mean?","answer":"to watch over people to make sure they are safe and doing things correctly","explanation":"Vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"يشرف على.","options":["to read very fast","to watch over people to make sure they are safe and doing things correctly","to write a letter","to pay for something"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*Twenty-four students **volunteered** to participate.* *Volunteered* means ___.","answer":"offered to help without being paid","explanation":"Context.","explanation_ar":"تطوعوا.","options":["offered to help without being paid","were forced to help","refused to help","were paid to help"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"How should a theme be written?","answer":"as a full sentence about life","explanation":"Theme.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة.","options":["as one word","as a full sentence about life","as a question","as a list of names"],"dok":1,"skill":"theme"},{"q":"Which sentence about the two texts is correct?","answer":"Both texts show how students can help their school.","explanation":"both + plural.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Both text shows how students can help their school.","Both texts shows how students can help their school.","Both of text show how students can help their school.","Both texts show how students can help their school."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"How does a formal letter usually share its message?","answer":"It states it directly through reasons and benefits.","explanation":"Genre.","explanation_ar":"يصرّح به مباشرة.","options":["It states it directly through reasons and benefits.","It hides it in dialogue.","It shows it only through pictures.","It never has a message."],"dok":2,"skill":"comparing texts"},{"q":"Which evidence from the story supports the theme of teamwork?","answer":"\"We made it grow together.\"","explanation":"Evidence.","explanation_ar":"الدليل.","options":["The roof was flat and empty.","\"We made it grow together.\"","Ms. Nouf asked three questions.","Hessa laughed."],"dok":2,"skill":"supporting evidence"},{"q":"Which is a TOPIC, not a theme?","answer":"a rooftop garden","explanation":"Topic vs. theme.","explanation_ar":"موضوع.","options":["a rooftop garden","Teamwork turns ideas into reality.","Young people can change their communities.","Careful plans help ideas succeed."],"dok":2,"skill":"theme"},{"q":"Why is it useful to compare the themes of two different texts?","answer":"It helps you see a big idea from different points of view and understand it more deeply.","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"لفهم الفكرة بعمق من زوايا مختلفة.","options":["It makes reading faster.","It shows which text is longer.","It helps you see a big idea from different points of view and understand it more deeply.","It replaces reading the texts."],"dok":3,"skill":"comparing texts"},{"q":"Which detail shows that Yara, like Dana, planned carefully?","answer":"She gave times, a supervising teacher and a date to review progress.","explanation":"Compare.","explanation_ar":"حددت الأوقات والإشراف وموعد المراجعة.","options":["She wrote her name at the end.","She visited Grade 3 once.","She used the word Dear.","She gave times, a supervising teacher and a date to review progress."],"dok":3,"skill":"comparing texts"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'program': a schedule with activities"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'supervise': a teacher watching students read"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'volunteer': students raising their hands to help"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'proposal': a document with 'Proposal' on the cover"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'grateful': a student smiling and saying thank you"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'patience': an older student calmly helping a younger one"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'message': a speech bubble with a heart"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-01","prompt":"Older and younger students reading together."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-02","prompt":"The parts of a formal letter."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS3-03","prompt":"A bridge showing a shared theme."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V01","script":"program. Reading Buddies is a new school program."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V02","script":"supervise. Ms. Lama will supervise the program."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V03","script":"volunteer. Twenty-four students volunteered."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V04","script":"proposal. Thank you for considering our proposal."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V05","script":"grateful. I would be grateful for your help."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V06","script":"patience. Reading with younger children takes patience."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-V07","script":"message. The letter's message is that students can help each other."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-T1","script":"**To:** The School Council, Al-Noor Intermediate School · **From:** Yara Al-Harbi, Class Representative, Grade 7B · **Date:** October 10 · **Subject:** Request to start a Reading Buddies program Dear Members of the School Council, I am writing to request your approval for a new program called Reading Buddies. In this program, students from Grade 7 would read with students from Grade 3 for twenty minutes, twice a week, during the morning activity period. Last month, our class visited the Grade 3 classrooms and listened to the children read. We noticed that many of them enjoy stories but still find long words difficult. At the same time, several of my classmates told me that they wanted to do something useful for our school community. Reading Buddies would benefit both groups. The younger students would get extra reading practice and a friendly older student to encourage them. The older students would develop patience, leadership and communication skills. In addition, the program would cost almost nothing, because we would use books from the school library. So far, twenty-four students from Grade 7 have volunteered to participate, and Ms. Lama, our English teacher, has kindly agreed to supervise the program. We would like to start in November and review our progress in January. I would be grateful if the council could approve this request at its next meeting. I would also be happy to present our plan in person and answer any questions. Thank you very much for taking the time to consider our proposal. Sincerely, Yara Al-Harbi Class Representative, Grade 7B"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS3-VID","script":"A garden on a roof. Reading buddies in the classroom. Two different texts – one big idea? Dear Members of the School Council, I am writing to request your approval for a new program called Reading Buddies… The story SHOWS its theme through events and characters. The letter STATES its message through reasons. Both texts: notice a need → plan carefully → work with others → make a difference! Write the theme as a sentence, support it with evidence – and compare!"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS4","title":"Writing Skill: Formal letter of request","lesson_type":"writing_skill","objectives":["identify the parts and features of a formal letter of request","use polite request language and a formal tone (no contractions, idioms or slang)","write a clear purpose, specific details and a formal closing"],"objectives_ar":["تحديد أجزاء رسالة الطلب الرسمية وسماتها.","استخدام لغة الطلب المهذبة والأسلوب الرسمي (دون اختصارات أو تعابير اصطلاحية أو عامية).","كتابة غرض واضح وتفاصيل محددة وخاتمة رسمية."],"success_criteria":["I can label the header, greeting, purpose, details, request, closing and signature.","I can rewrite informal sentences in a formal tone.","I can write a purpose sentence and a polite request with specific details."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع تسمية الترويسة والتحية والغرض والتفاصيل والطلب والخاتمة والتوقيع.","أستطيع إعادة كتابة الجمل غير الرسمية بأسلوب رسمي.","أستطيع كتابة جملة غرض وطلب مهذب بتفاصيل محددة."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"formal","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈfɔrməl/","definition":"serious and polite, used in official situations","arabic":"رسمي","example":"Use formal language in a letter to the principal.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"on behalf of","pos":"phrase","ipa":"/ɑn bɪˈhæf ʌv/","definition":"for or as the representative of someone","arabic":"نيابةً عن","example":"I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"consideration","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kənˌsɪdəˈreɪʃən/","definition":"careful thought about something","arabic":"اعتبار / نظر","example":"Thank you for your time and consideration.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"subject line","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsʌbdʒɪkt ˌlaɪn/","definition":"a short line that tells the reader what a letter or email is about","arabic":"سطر الموضوع","example":"Write a clear subject line.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"contraction","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kənˈtrækʃən/","definition":"a short form of two words, such as *I'm* or *don't*","arabic":"صيغة مختصرة","example":"Avoid contractions in formal letters.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"in return","pos":"phrase","ipa":"/ɪn rɪˈtɝn/","definition":"as a way of thanking or paying back","arabic":"في المقابل","example":"In return, we will display your name.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"sincerely","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/sɪnˈsɪrli/","definition":"honestly; used to end a formal letter","arabic":"مع خالص التحية / بإخلاص","example":"End your letter with *Sincerely,*","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **formal letter of request** politely asks a person in an official position – a principal, a manager, a council – for **permission, help or a donation**. Its parts: **header** (To, From, Date, Subject) → **greeting** (*Dear Ms. Nouf,* / *Dear Members of the School Council,*) → **purpose** → **details** → **request** → **closing** → **signature** (full name and role).\n\nBegin with the **purpose**: *I am writing to request… / I am writing on behalf of… to ask whether…*. Then give **specific details**: **who, what, when, where, why** and **how much**. Explain the **benefits** for the reader or the community. Make the request **politely**: *Would it be possible…? / I would be grateful if… / Could you please…?*\n\nKeep the **tone formal**: **no contractions** (*I am*, not *I'm*), **no idioms or slang** (*participate*, not *pitch in*), **no emojis**, full sentences. Close with thanks: *Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to hearing from you. Sincerely,*","examples":["Subject line: ***Request for a donation of seeds and pots***","Greeting: ***Dear Mr. Al-Shehri,*** / ***Dear Members of the School Council,***","Purpose: ***I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club … to ask whether your garden center would be able to donate…***","Details: ***We would need about fifty small pots and a few packets of mint, basil and sidr seeds.***","Benefit: ***The garden will provide shade, teach students about plants and supply fresh mint for our canteen.***","Polite request: ***Would it be possible to collect the donation before November 20?***","Offer in return: ***In return, we would be pleased to display your company's name on a thank-you sign.***","Closing: ***Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to hearing from you.***","Informal → formal: *Hey! Can u give us some stuff?* → ***I would be grateful if you could donate some materials.***"],"common_errors":["✗ Hi Mr. Fahad! → ✓ Dear Mr. Al-Shehri, (Formal greeting + family name + comma.)","✗ I'm writing because we wanna… → ✓ I am writing because we would like to… (No contractions or slang.)","✗ Give us 50 pots. → ✓ Would it be possible to donate fifty pots? (Polite request language.)","✗ Starting with a long story before the request. → ✓ State your purpose in the first paragraph. (Purpose first.)","✗ We need some stuff soon. → ✓ We would need about fifty small pots before November 20. (Specific details.)","✗ Everyone will pitch in! → ✓ All thirty members will participate. (No idioms.)","✗ Bye! See you! → ✓ Thank you for your time and consideration. Sincerely, (Formal closing.)"],"arabic":"رسالة الطلب الرسمية تطلب بأدب من شخص في موقع رسمي (مدير، مسؤول متجر، مجلس) إذنًا أو مساعدة أو تبرعًا، وأجزاؤها: الترويسة، ثم التحية، ثم الغرض، ثم التفاصيل، ثم الطلب، ثم الخاتمة، ثم التوقيع.\n\nابدأ بالغرض: I am writing to request…، ثم قدّم تفاصيل محددة (من، ماذا، متى، أين، لماذا، كم)، واشرح الفوائد، واطلب بأدب: Would it be possible…? / I would be grateful if…\n\nحافظ على الأسلوب الرسمي: لا صيغ مختصرة (I am لا I'm)، ولا تعابير اصطلاحية أو عامية، ولا رموز تعبيرية، واختم بالشكر وSincerely.\n\nانتبه: التحية الرسمية Dear + اللقب + اسم العائلة + فاصلة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:30","narration":"Hey, give us stuff! – or – Would it be possible to donate…? Which one gets a YES?","on_screen":"Writing a Formal Letter of Request ✉️","visual":"Two letters: one messy with emojis, one neat and formal."},{"time":"00:30–01:40","narration":"Dear Mr. Al-Shehri, I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club…","on_screen":"(model letter)","visual":"Majed at a desk; the garden center; seed packets and pots."},{"time":"01:40–02:40","narration":"Header, greeting, purpose, details, request, closing, signature – every part has a job!","on_screen":"7 parts of a formal letter","visual":"Each part of the letter lights up with a label."},{"time":"02:40–03:30","narration":"Would it be possible…? I would be grateful if… – polite words open doors!","on_screen":"Polite request language","visual":"A door opens as each polite phrase appears."},{"time":"03:30–04:00","narration":"No contractions, no idioms, no emojis – just clear, polite, formal English.","on_screen":"Formal tone ✔","visual":"I'm → I am; pitch in → participate; 😊 → removed."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أعطونا أشياء! أم: هل يمكن التبرع بـ…؟ أيهما ينال الموافقة؟","السيد الشهري المحترم، أكتب إليكم نيابةً عن نادي البيئة…","الترويسة والتحية والغرض والتفاصيل والطلب والخاتمة والتوقيع: لكل جزء وظيفة!","Would it be possible… وI would be grateful if… الكلمات المهذبة تفتح الأبواب!","لا صيغ مختصرة، ولا تعابير اصطلاحية، ولا رموز تعبيرية: إنجليزية رسمية واضحة ومهذبة فقط."],"voice":"Narrator: American English, professional but friendly male voice, speed 1.0. Majed reads his letter."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"A Formal Letter of Request (by Majed)","body":"**To:** Mr. Fahad Al-Shehri, Manager, Green Valley Garden Center · **From:** Majed Al-Qahtani, President of the Eco Club, Al-Noor Intermediate School · **Date:** November 3 · **Subject:** Request for a donation of seeds and pots\n\nDear Mr. Al-Shehri,\n\nI am writing on behalf of the Eco Club at Al-Noor Intermediate School to ask whether your garden center would be able to donate some seeds and small pots for our new school garden.\n\nOur club has thirty members, and we are planning to grow herbs and native plants in the school courtyard. The garden will provide shade, teach students about plants and supply fresh mint for our canteen. We would need about fifty small pots and a few packets of mint, basil and sidr seeds.\n\nWould it be possible to collect the donation before November 20? In return, we would be pleased to display your company's name on a thank-you sign in the garden.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to hearing from you.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMajed Al-Qahtani\n\nPresident, Eco Club","word_count":170,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L06-U6-LS4-1","genre":"letter/email","role":"model","difficulty":"700L–850L","glossary":[],"annotations":["**Header:** who it is to, who it is from, the date and a clear **subject line**.","**Formal greeting:** *Dear Mr. Al-Shehri,* – title + family name + comma.","**Purpose first:** *I am writing … to ask whether…* – the reader knows the request at once.","**Details:** who (thirty members), what (fifty pots, seeds), why (shade, learning, fresh mint), when (before November 20).","**Polite request language:** *Would it be possible…? / we would be pleased to…*","**Formal tone:** no contractions (*I am*, not *I'm*), no idioms, no slang, no emojis.","**Closing:** thanks + *I look forward to hearing from you.* + *Sincerely,* + full name and role."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Majed's letter. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ رسالة ماجد واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"To whom is Majed writing?","answer":"Mr. Fahad Al-Shehri, the manager of a garden center","explanation":"Header.","explanation_ar":"مدير مركز الحدائق.","options":["the school principal","his teacher","a friend in another school","Mr. Fahad Al-Shehri, the manager of a garden center"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What is Majed requesting?","answer":"a donation of seeds and small pots","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"التبرع ببذور وأصص.","options":["permission to use the roof","money for a trip","a job at the garden center","a donation of seeds and small pots"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How many members does the Eco Club have?","answer":"thirty","explanation":"Details.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثون.","options":["fifty","twenty","thirty","twelve"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"When would the club like to collect the donation?","answer":"before November 20","explanation":"Details.","explanation_ar":"قبل 20 نوفمبر.","options":["before November 20","on November 3","next year","at the end of the term"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What does Majed offer in return?","answer":"to display the company's name on a thank-you sign","explanation":"In return.","explanation_ar":"عرض اسم الشركة على لافتة شكر.","options":["to display the company's name on a thank-you sign","to pay for the seeds","to work at the garden center","to send flowers"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which part of Majed's letter states the PURPOSE?","answer":"I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club … to ask whether your garden center would be able to donate…","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"جملة الغرض.","options":["Sincerely,","I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club … to ask whether your garden center would be able to donate…","Thank you for your time and consideration.","Our club has thirty members."],"dok":2,"skill":"letter structure","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS4-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Formal letters. Choose.","instructions_ar":"الرسائل الرسمية: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which greeting is correct for a formal letter to the principal, Ms. Nouf Al-Otaibi?","answer":"Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi,","explanation":"Formal greeting.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi,","Hey Ms. Nouf!","Hi teacher,","Yo Principal,"],"dok":1,"skill":"letter format","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence has a FORMAL tone?","answer":"I would be grateful if you could approve our request.","explanation":"Tone.","explanation_ar":"رسمية.","options":["Please say yes, it's gonna be awesome!","We really really need this, OK?","I would be grateful if you could approve our request.","Give us the room tomorrow."],"dok":2,"skill":"formal language","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which is the BEST polite request for the use of the school hall?","answer":"Would it be possible to use the school hall on Thursday afternoon?","explanation":"Polite request.","explanation_ar":"أفضل طلب مهذب.","options":["We want the hall Thursday.","Would it be possible to use the school hall on Thursday afternoon?","Give us the hall.","The hall is ours on Thursday."],"dok":2,"skill":"polite requests","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about the donation avoids contractions correctly?","answer":"We do not need large pots.","explanation":"No contractions.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["We don't need large pots.","We do not need large pots.","We dont need large pots.","We'd not need large pots."],"dok":2,"skill":"formal language","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which detail is the MOST specific for a request letter?","answer":"We would need fifty small pots before November 20.","explanation":"Specific details.","explanation_ar":"الأكثر تحديدًا.","options":["We need some pots soon.","We need lots of things.","We need stuff for the garden.","We would need fifty small pots before November 20."],"dok":2,"skill":"details","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which is the BEST closing for a formal letter of request?","answer":"Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to hearing from you. Sincerely,","explanation":"Closing.","explanation_ar":"أفضل خاتمة.","options":["Bye for now! 😊","That's it. See ya,","Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to hearing from you. Sincerely,","Love,"],"dok":3,"skill":"letter format","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS4-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete the formal letter with the word bank.","instructions_ar":"أكمل الرسالة الرسمية من بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"________ Members of the School Council,","answer":"Dear","explanation":"Greeting.","explanation_ar":"الأعزاء / المحترمون.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"I am writing on ________ of the Reading Club to request a new bookshelf.","answer":"behalf","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"نيابةً.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Would it be ________ to place it in the library corner?","answer":"possible","explanation":"Polite request.","explanation_ar":"ممكنًا.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"I would be ________ if you could approve this request.","answer":"grateful","explanation":"Polite request.","explanation_ar":"ممتنًا.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Thank you for your time and ________.","answer":"consideration","explanation":"Closing.","explanation_ar":"اعتباركم.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________,","answer":"Sincerely","explanation":"Sign-off.","explanation_ar":"مع خالص التحية.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS4-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write formal requests.","instructions_ar":"اكتب طلبات رسمية.","items":[{"q":"Rewrite formally: *Hey! Can we use the gym on Thursday? It'll be fun!*","answer":"Dear Mr. Saleh, I am writing to ask whether our class could use the gym on Thursday afternoon for a sports event.","explanation":"Formal.","explanation_ar":"رسمي.","dok":2,"skill":"formal language","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a subject line and a purpose sentence for a letter asking a local bakery to donate bread for a charity event.","answer":"Subject: Request for a donation of bread for a charity event. Purpose: I am writing on behalf of Grade 7 to ask whether your bakery would be able to donate bread for our charity breakfast on December 5.","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"الغرض.","dok":2,"skill":"letter structure","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write two specific details and one benefit for your bakery request.","answer":"We would need about one hundred loaves, and we would collect them at 7 a.m. The breakfast will raise money for families in need in our neighborhood.","explanation":"Details.","explanation_ar":"التفاصيل.","dok":3,"skill":"details","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a polite request and a formal closing for your bakery letter.","answer":"Would it be possible to confirm the donation by November 30? Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to hearing from you. Sincerely, Majed Al-Qahtani","explanation":"Request + closing.","explanation_ar":"الطلب والخاتمة.","dok":2,"skill":"letter format","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Formal or Not?","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Letter editor: an informal letter appears with highlighted words; the child taps each informal word and chooses the formal replacement. A fully formal letter flies into the manager's inbox and gets an 'APPROVED' stamp.","The teacher reads a sentence card.","Teams raise green (formal) or red (informal).","For red cards, the team must say a formal version.","Correct formal sentences are posted in the letter box.","Correct paddle = 1 point; good formal version = 2 points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is a *formal letter of request*?","answer":"a polite letter asking someone in an official position for help or permission","explanation":"Definition.","explanation_ar":"رسالة طلب رسمية.","options":["a polite letter asking someone in an official position for help or permission","a letter to a friend about your holiday","a funny story","a list of rules"],"dok":1,"skill":"genre"},{"q":"What is a *contraction*?","answer":"a short form of two words, such as *I'm* or *don't*","explanation":"Vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"صيغة مختصرة.","options":["a long formal word","a short form of two words, such as *I'm* or *don't*","a kind of greeting","the subject line"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*I am writing **on behalf of** the Eco Club.* This means ___.","answer":"as the representative of the club","explanation":"Context.","explanation_ar":"نيابةً عن النادي.","options":["against the club","instead of joining the club","as the representative of the club","about the club's history"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Where should you state the PURPOSE of a formal letter?","answer":"in the first paragraph","explanation":"Structure.","explanation_ar":"في الفقرة الأولى.","options":["in the first paragraph","only in the signature","at the very end","in the subject line only"],"dok":1,"skill":"letter structure"},{"q":"Which sentence for a formal letter is correct?","answer":"I would be grateful if you could reply by Monday.","explanation":"Formal + grammar.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["I'd be grateful if u could reply by Monday.","Reply by Monday, OK?","I would be grateful if you could reply by Monday.","I would grateful if you could reply by Monday."],"dok":2,"skill":"formal language"},{"q":"Which phrase makes a request MORE polite?","answer":"Would it be possible to…","explanation":"Polite request.","explanation_ar":"أكثر تهذيبًا.","options":["Would it be possible to…","Give me…","I want…","You must…"],"dok":2,"skill":"polite requests"},{"q":"Why should a formal letter avoid idioms like *pitch in*?","answer":"Idioms are informal; formal letters need clear, serious language.","explanation":"Tone.","explanation_ar":"لأنها غير رسمية.","options":["Idioms are always wrong English.","Idioms make letters too short.","Managers don't know any idioms.","Idioms are informal; formal letters need clear, serious language."],"dok":2,"skill":"formal language"},{"q":"Which detail makes a request letter MORE convincing?","answer":"a clear benefit for the community","explanation":"Persuasion.","explanation_ar":"فائدة واضحة للمجتمع.","options":["a joke about the manager","a clear benefit for the community","a long story about your weekend","many exclamation marks"],"dok":2,"skill":"details"},{"q":"A student's letter starts *Hi Fahad! We need pots.* What is the BEST advice?","answer":"Use a formal greeting with the family name and a polite purpose sentence.","explanation":"Revising.","explanation_ar":"تحية رسمية وجملة غرض مهذبة.","options":["Add emojis to be friendly.","Use a formal greeting with the family name and a polite purpose sentence.","Make the letter longer with a story.","Remove the request completely."],"dok":3,"skill":"revising"},{"q":"Why does Majed offer to display the company's name on a sign?","answer":"to thank the company and make the request more attractive","explanation":"Persuasion.","explanation_ar":"شكرًا وترغيبًا.","options":["to sell the seeds","to ask for more money","to advertise the school","to thank the company and make the request more attractive"],"dok":3,"skill":"persuasion"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'formal': a neat letter with a school logo"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'on behalf of': a student speaking for a group"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'consideration': a manager reading a letter carefully"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'subject line': an email with the subject line highlighted"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'contraction': I'm → I am written on a card"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'in return': two hands exchanging gifts"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'sincerely': a signature under the word Sincerely"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-01","prompt":"A student writing a formal letter of request."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-02","prompt":"The seven parts of a formal letter."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS4-03","prompt":"Informal language changed into formal language."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V01","script":"formal. Use formal language in a letter to the principal."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V02","script":"on behalf of. I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V03","script":"consideration. Thank you for your time and consideration."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V04","script":"subject line. Write a clear subject line."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V05","script":"contraction. Avoid contractions in formal letters."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V06","script":"in return. In return, we will display your name."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-V07","script":"sincerely. End your letter with *Sincerely,*"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-T1","script":"**To:** Mr. Fahad Al-Shehri, Manager, Green Valley Garden Center · **From:** Majed Al-Qahtani, President of the Eco Club, Al-Noor Intermediate School · **Date:** November 3 · **Subject:** Request for a donation of seeds and pots Dear Mr. Al-Shehri, I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club at Al-Noor Intermediate School to ask whether your garden center would be able to donate some seeds and small pots for our new school garden. Our club has thirty members, and we are planning to grow herbs and native plants in the school courtyard. The garden will provide shade, teach students about plants and supply fresh mint for our canteen. We would need about fifty small pots and a few packets of mint, basil and sidr seeds. Would it be possible to collect the donation before November 20? In return, we would be pleased to display your company's name on a thank-you sign in the garden. Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to hearing from you. Sincerely, Majed Al-Qahtani President, Eco Club"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Hey, give us stuff! – or – Would it be possible to donate…? Which one gets a YES? Dear Mr. Al-Shehri, I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club… Header, greeting, purpose, details, request, closing, signature – every part has a job! Would it be possible…? I would be grateful if… – polite words open doors! No contractions, no idioms, no emojis – just clear, polite, formal English."}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS5","title":"Writing Workshop: A formal letter proposing a school project","lesson_type":"writing_workshop","objectives":["plan a formal letter proposing a school project with the Proposal Letter Planner","write 150–200 words with a formal greeting, a clear purpose, specific details and benefits, a polite request and a formal closing","revise, edit and 'send' the letter to the class School Council for a vote"],"objectives_ar":["التخطيط لرسالة رسمية تقترح مشروعًا مدرسيًا بمخطط رسالة المقترح.","كتابة 150–200 كلمة بتحية رسمية وغرض واضح وتفاصيل وفوائد محددة وطلب مهذب وخاتمة رسمية.","تحسين الرسالة وتدقيقها و«إرسالها» إلى مجلس المدرسة الصفي للتصويت."],"success_criteria":["My first paragraph states what I propose and why.","My second paragraph gives specific details (who, when, where, cost) and benefits for the school or community.","My third paragraph makes a polite request and closes formally; the whole letter is formal and 150–200 words."],"success_criteria_ar":["فقرتي الأولى تذكر ما أقترحه ولماذا.","فقرتي الثانية تقدّم تفاصيل محددة وفوائد للمدرسة أو المجتمع.","فقرتي الثالثة تتضمن طلبًا مهذبًا وخاتمة رسمية، والرسالة كلها رسمية في 150–200 كلمة."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"charity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃærəti/","definition":"an organization or an activity that helps people in need","arabic":"عمل خيري / جمعية خيرية","example":"The book fair is a charity event.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"resident","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɛzɪdənt/","definition":"a person who lives in a particular place","arabic":"مقيم / ساكن","example":"The residents of the care home enjoyed the visit.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"care home","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɛr ˌhoʊm/","definition":"a place where elderly people live and are looked after","arabic":"دار رعاية المسنين","example":"We visited a care home in our city.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"permission","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pərˈmɪʃən/","definition":"the act of allowing someone to do something","arabic":"إذن","example":"We need permission to use the hall.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"supplier","pos":"noun","ipa":"/səˈplaɪər/","definition":"a company that sells or provides goods","arabic":"مورّد","example":"The supplier's price is 4,000 riyals.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"loneliness","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈloʊnlinəs/","definition":"the sad feeling of being alone","arabic":"الوحدة","example":"Kindness Week can reduce loneliness.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"vote","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/voʊt/","definition":"to choose officially by raising hands or writing on a paper","arabic":"يصوّت / تصويت","example":"The class council will vote on the proposals.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **proposal letter** suggests a **new project** and asks for **approval**. It must be **clear**, **specific** and **persuasive** – but always **polite and formal**. Begin with a formal **greeting**: *Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi,*\n\n**Paragraph 1 – Purpose:** what you propose and why (*I am writing to propose… because…*). **Paragraph 2 – Details and benefits:** **who** will do it, **when** and **where**, what it will **cost** and how you will pay, and **how it will benefit** students or the community – use facts from your planning card. **Paragraph 3 – Request:** ask politely for approval (*I would be grateful if you could approve…*), offer to answer questions and thank the reader. End with *Sincerely,* + your full name and class.\n\nFormal tone: **no contractions, idioms, slang or emojis**. Use **would** for plans (*students would sell books*), **linking words** (*In addition, As a result, Therefore*) and specific **numbers and dates**. Keep the letter (greeting to signature) **150–200 words**.","examples":["Greeting: ***Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi,***","Purpose: ***I am writing on behalf of Grade 7 to propose a Charity Book Fair at our school.***","Why: ***The money we raise would buy new books for the children's library at our local hospital.***","Details: ***The fair would take place in the school hall on Thursday, February 12, from 12:00 to 3:00.***","Who: ***Thirty Grade 7 volunteers and two teachers would run the fair.***","Benefit: ***In addition, students would find new books to read at a very low price.***","Request: ***I would be grateful if you could give us permission to use the hall and to send a letter to parents asking for books.***","Offer + thanks: ***I would be happy to answer any questions. Thank you for your time and consideration.***","Sign-off: ***Sincerely, Yara Al-Harbi, Grade 7B***"],"common_errors":["✗ Hi Ms. Nouf! We want a book fair! → ✓ Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi, I am writing to propose a book fair. (Formal greeting and purpose.)","✗ We'll sell books and it'll be awesome. → ✓ We would sell donated books for five riyals each. (No contractions or slang; be specific.)","✗ No details about time or place. → ✓ Give the date, time and place. (Who, when, where, cost.)","✗ Forgetting the benefits. → ✓ Explain how the project helps students or the community. (Benefits persuade.)","✗ Approve our fair now. → ✓ I would be grateful if you could approve our fair. (Polite request.)","✗ Everyone will chip in! → ✓ All thirty volunteers will participate. (No idioms.)","✗ Writing 250 words. → ✓ Keep it 150–200 words. (Check the length.)"],"arabic":"رسالة المقترح تقترح مشروعًا جديدًا وتطلب الموافقة عليه، ويجب أن تكون واضحة ومحددة ومقنعة، لكنها مهذبة ورسمية دائمًا، وتبدأ بتحية رسمية.\n\nالفقرة الأولى: الغرض (ما تقترحه ولماذا). الثانية: التفاصيل والفوائد (من، متى، أين، التكلفة، وكيف يفيد الطلاب أو المجتمع). الثالثة: طلب الموافقة بأدب، وعرض الإجابة عن الأسئلة، والشكر، ثم Sincerely والاسم الكامل والصف.\n\nالأسلوب الرسمي: دون صيغ مختصرة أو تعابير اصطلاحية أو عامية أو رموز تعبيرية، واستخدم would للخطط، وكلمات الربط، والأرقام والتواريخ المحددة، والتزم بطول 150–200 كلمة.\n\nانتبه: الفوائد الواضحة تجعل الطلب أكثر إقناعًا."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:30","narration":"You have an idea that could make a difference. Now – how do you get the principal to say yes?","on_screen":"My Proposal Letter ✉️🏫","visual":"A student holds a project card and walks toward the principal's office."},{"time":"00:30–01:20","narration":"A refill station, a charity book fair, a visit to a care home, a Kindness Week – which project will you propose?","on_screen":"Project Cards A–D","visual":"Four cards appear with icons."},{"time":"01:20–02:40","narration":"Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi, I am writing on behalf of Grade 7 to propose a Charity Book Fair…","on_screen":"(model letter)","visual":"Book donations, a school hall with tables, children reading new books in a hospital library."},{"time":"02:40–03:30","narration":"Purpose. Details and benefits. A polite request. Formal from 'Dear' to 'Sincerely'!","on_screen":"P1 Purpose · P2 Details + benefits · P3 Request","visual":"Three envelope flaps open one by one."},{"time":"03:30–04:00","narration":"Send your letter to our class School Council – and let the vote begin!","on_screen":"School Council vote 🗳️","visual":"Students raise hands; a stamp says APPROVED."}],"captions_ar":["لديك فكرة قد تُحدث فرقًا. فكيف تجعل المديرة توافق؟","محطة تعبئة مياه، أو معرض كتب خيري، أو زيارة دار رعاية، أو أسبوع اللطف: أي مشروع ستقترح؟","المديرة الفاضلة، أكتب إليكم نيابةً عن الصف السابع لأقترح معرضًا خيريًا للكتب…","الغرض، ثم التفاصيل والفوائد، ثم الطلب المهذب، وأسلوب رسمي من التحية إلى التوقيع!","أرسل رسالتك إلى مجلس المدرسة الصفي، وليبدأ التصويت!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, encouraging female voice, speed 1.0. A student reads the model letter."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"School Project Planning Cards","body":"**Card A – Water Refill Station** · What: a water refill station near the canteen · Why: students buy many small plastic bottles every day; a station would reduce plastic waste and keep students drinking water · Cost: about 4,000 riyals (supplier's price) · How to pay: a recycling drive and a class fundraiser · Who: the Eco Club (25 members) · When: ready before the hot season in April\n\n**Card B – Charity Book Fair** · What: a one-day fair selling donated used books for 5 riyals each · Why: money will buy new books for the children's library at the local hospital; students will also find books to read · Where: the school hall · When: Thursday, February 12, from 12:00 to 3:00 · Who: Grade 7 volunteers (30 students) and two teachers · Needs: permission to use the hall and to send a letter to parents asking for books\n\n**Card C – Elderly Visit Day** · What: a visit to a local care home for elderly people · Why: many residents rarely have visitors; students can read, talk and share Arabic coffee and dates with them · Who: 20 students from Grade 7 with three teachers · When: a Tuesday morning in March · Needs: permission, the school bus and parents' signed forms\n\n**Card D – Kindness Week** · What: a week of kindness activities: a compliment wall, a buddy bench in the playground and older students helping younger ones at lunch · Why: to make every student feel welcome and to reduce loneliness · When: the first week of the second term · Needs: permission and a small budget of 300 riyals for materials","word_count":256,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L06-U6-LS5-1","genre":"project cards","role":"model","difficulty":"700L–850L","glossary":[],"annotations":["Choose **one project card**. You will write a **formal letter** to the principal to **propose** the project and **request** approval.","Plan **three paragraphs** after the greeting: (1) purpose – what you propose and why; (2) details and benefits – who, when, where, cost; (3) the request and thanks.","Keep the tone **formal**: no contractions, idioms, slang or emojis. Begin with *Dear …,* and end with *Sincerely,* and your full name and class."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS5-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the project cards and the model. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ بطاقات المشاريع والنموذج واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"How much would the water refill station cost, according to Card A?","answer":"about 4,000 riyals","explanation":"Card A.","explanation_ar":"نحو 4000 ريال.","options":["about 300 riyals","5 riyals","about 40,000 riyals","about 4,000 riyals"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What would the money from the Charity Book Fair buy?","answer":"new books for the children's library at the local hospital","explanation":"Card B.","explanation_ar":"كتبًا جديدة لمكتبة الأطفال في المستشفى.","options":["new books for the children's library at the local hospital","a new school bus","a buddy bench","a water refill station"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What do students need for Elderly Visit Day?","answer":"permission, the school bus and parents' signed forms","explanation":"Card C.","explanation_ar":"الإذن والحافلة ونماذج أولياء الأمور.","options":["a refill station","a budget of 4,000 riyals","permission, the school bus and parents' signed forms","the school hall"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which project includes a compliment wall and a buddy bench?","answer":"Kindness Week","explanation":"Card D.","explanation_ar":"أسبوع اللطف.","options":["Charity Book Fair","Water Refill Station","Kindness Week","Elderly Visit Day"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"In the model letter, how many volunteers would run the book fair?","answer":"thirty Grade 7 volunteers and two teachers","explanation":"Details.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثون متطوعًا ومعلمتان.","options":["twelve students","thirty Grade 7 volunteers and two teachers","the whole school","only Yara"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which part of the model letter makes the REQUEST?","answer":"I would be grateful if you could give us permission to use the hall…","explanation":"Request.","explanation_ar":"جملة الطلب.","options":["The fair would take place in the school hall…","Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi,","Sincerely,","I would be grateful if you could give us permission to use the hall…"],"dok":2,"skill":"letter structure","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS5-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Plan your proposal letter. Choose.","instructions_ar":"خطّط لرسالة المقترح: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which is the BEST purpose sentence for a letter about Card A?","answer":"I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club to propose a water refill station near the canteen.","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"أفضل جملة غرض.","options":["I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club to propose a water refill station near the canteen.","Water is very important for everyone.","Hi! We want water!","The canteen is near the gym."],"dok":2,"skill":"letter structure","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence gives the MOST specific details for Elderly Visit Day?","answer":"Twenty Grade 7 students and three teachers would visit the care home on a Tuesday morning in March.","explanation":"Specific details.","explanation_ar":"الأكثر تحديدًا.","options":["Some students would go somewhere soon.","We want to visit old people.","Twenty Grade 7 students and three teachers would visit the care home on a Tuesday morning in March.","It would be a nice day."],"dok":2,"skill":"details","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence explains a BENEFIT of Kindness Week?","answer":"It would help every student feel welcome and reduce loneliness.","explanation":"Benefit.","explanation_ar":"فائدة.","options":["It would take place in the first week of the second term.","It would help every student feel welcome and reduce loneliness.","It would need 300 riyals.","It would need permission."],"dok":2,"skill":"benefits","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about the refill station keeps a formal tone?","answer":"The station would reduce plastic waste significantly.","explanation":"Formal tone.","explanation_ar":"رسمية.","options":["The station'd be super cool!","The station would reduce plastic waste significantly.","Everybody's gonna love it.","It'll save tons of bottles, LOL."],"dok":2,"skill":"formal language","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *would* correctly to describe a plan?","answer":"Volunteers would sell each book for five riyals.","explanation":"would + base verb.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Volunteers would sell each book for five riyals.","Volunteers would sells each book for five riyals.","Volunteers would to sell each book for five riyals.","Volunteers would selling each book for five riyals."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar","stage":"guided"},{"q":"The principal might worry about the cost of the refill station. Which sentence BEST answers this concern?","answer":"We would raise the money through a recycling drive and a class fundraiser, so the school would not need to pay.","explanation":"Answering concerns.","explanation_ar":"أفضل إجابة عن القلق.","options":["Money is not important.","Please don't worry about it.","The station is blue.","We would raise the money through a recycling drive and a class fundraiser, so the school would not need to pay."],"dok":3,"skill":"persuasion","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS5-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Plan your letter with the Proposal Letter Planner.","instructions_ar":"خطط لرسالتك بمخطط رسالة المقترح.","items":[{"q":"Greeting and purpose for Card A.","answer":"Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi, I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club to propose a water refill station near the canteen, because students buy many small plastic bottles every day.","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"الغرض.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Details: who, when, where and cost.","answer":"the Eco Club (25 members); near the canteen; ready before April; about 4,000 riyals, paid by a recycling drive and a class fundraiser","explanation":"Details.","explanation_ar":"التفاصيل.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Two benefits.","answer":"It would reduce plastic waste, and it would encourage students to drink more water during the hot season.","explanation":"Benefits.","explanation_ar":"الفوائد.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Request and closing.","answer":"I would be grateful if you could approve the project so that we can order the station in March. Thank you for your time and consideration. Sincerely, [name], [class]","explanation":"Request.","explanation_ar":"الطلب.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS5-A4","type":"writing","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write, revise, edit and send your letter.","instructions_ar":"اكتب رسالتك وحسّنها ودققها وأرسلها.","items":[{"q":"Write the greeting and Paragraph 1 (purpose).","answer":"Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi, I am writing on behalf of the Eco Club to propose a water refill station near the canteen. Every day, students buy many small plastic bottles, and most of them end up in the trash.","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"الفقرة الأولى.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write Paragraph 2 (details and benefits).","answer":"The station would cost about 4,000 riyals, and our twenty-five members would raise the money through a recycling drive and a class fundraiser. It would be ready before the hot season in April. In addition to reducing plastic waste, it would encourage students to drink more water.","explanation":"Paragraph 2.","explanation_ar":"الفقرة الثانية.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write Paragraph 3 (request) and the formal closing.","answer":"I would be grateful if you could approve this project so that we can order the station in March. I would be happy to answer any questions. Thank you for your time and consideration. Sincerely, Majed Al-Qahtani, Grade 7A","explanation":"Paragraph 3.","explanation_ar":"الفقرة الثالثة.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write one sentence you changed from informal to formal (before → after).","answer":"Before: It'll be super cool and everyone will chip in! After: Many students would participate, and the project would benefit the whole school.","explanation":"Revision.","explanation_ar":"تحسين.","dok":3,"skill":"revising","stage":"production","_w":{"checklist":[],"min":null,"max":null}}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS5-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Proposal Letter Planner","instructions":"Organizer: Choose one card. Plan each part of your letter in formal language.","items":[{"q":"Greeting","answer":"Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi,"},{"q":"Purpose: what I propose and why","answer":"a Charity Book Fair – money for new books for the hospital children's library"},{"q":"Details: who, when, where, cost","answer":"30 Grade 7 volunteers + 2 teachers; school hall; Thursday, February 12, 12:00–3:00; books sold for 5 riyals"},{"q":"Benefits for students or the community","answer":"children in hospital get new books; students find books cheaply; we reuse books"},{"q":"Polite request + offer to answer questions","answer":"I would be grateful if you could approve the use of the hall and a letter to parents; happy to answer questions"},{"q":"Formal closing and signature","answer":"Thank you for your time and consideration. Sincerely, Yara Al-Harbi, Grade 7B"}]},{"id":"RW-L06-U6-LS5-WR","type":"writing","instructions":"Writing: Choose one School Project Planning Card. Write a formal letter (150–200 words) to the principal, Ms. Al-Otaibi, proposing the project. After the greeting, write three paragraphs: (1) what you propose and why; (2) specific details (who, when, where, cost) and the benefits; (3) a polite request for approval, an offer to answer questions and thanks. End with a formal closing and your name and class. Choose one School Project Planning Card. Write a formal letter (150–200 words) to the principal, Ms. Al-Otaibi, proposing the project. After the greeting, write three paragraphs: (1) what you propose and why; (2) specific details (who, when, where, cost) and the benefits; (3) a polite request for approval, an offer to answer questions and thanks. End with a formal closing and your name and class.","instructions_ar":"اختر بطاقة من بطاقات تخطيط المشاريع المدرسية، واكتب رسالة رسمية (150–200 كلمة) إلى المديرة الأستاذة العتيبي تقترح فيها المشروع. بعد التحية اكتب ثلاث فقرات: (1) ما تقترحه ولماذا، (2) التفاصيل المحددة (من، متى، أين، التكلفة) والفوائد، (3) طلبًا مهذبًا للموافقة مع عرض الإجابة عن الأسئلة والشكر، ثم اختم بخاتمة رسمية واسمك وصفك.","prompt":"Choose one School Project Planning Card. Write a formal letter (150–200 words) to the principal, Ms. Al-Otaibi, proposing the project. After the greeting, write three paragraphs: (1) what you propose and why; (2) specific details (who, when, where, cost) and the benefits; (3) a polite request for approval, an offer to answer questions and thanks. End with a formal closing and your name and class.","checklist":["I used a formal greeting with the principal's title and family name.","My first paragraph says what I propose and why.","I gave specific details: who, when, where and cost.","I explained at least two benefits for students or the community.","I made a polite request (Would it be possible… / I would be grateful if…).","I used no contractions, idioms, slang or emojis.","I ended with thanks, Sincerely, and my full name and class.","My letter is 150–200 words, and I checked spelling and punctuation."],"rubric_id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","min_words":150,"max_words":220,"organizer":"Proposal Letter Planner (greeting – purpose – details – benefits – request – closing)","items":[{"q":"Choose one School Project Planning Card. Write a formal letter (150–200 words) to the principal, Ms. Al-Otaibi, proposing the project. After the greeting, write three paragraphs: (1) what you propose and why; (2) specific details (who, when, where, cost) and the benefits; (3) a polite request for approval, an offer to answer questions and thanks. End with a formal closing and your name and class.","answer":"Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi, (new paragraph) I am writing on behalf of Grade 7 to propose a Charity Book Fair at our school. The money we raise would buy new books for the children's library at our local hospital, where many young patients spend long days with very little to read. (new paragraph) The fair would take place in the school hall on Thursday, February 12, from 12:00 to 3:00. Students and families would donate used books in good condition, and we would sell each book for five riyals. Thirty Grade 7 volunteers and two teachers have agreed to organize and run the fair. In addition to helping the hospital, the fair would allow students to find new books at a very low price and encourage everyone to reuse books instead of throwing them away. (new paragraph) I would be grateful if you could give us permission to use the hall and to send a letter to parents asking for books. I would be happy to answer any questions. Thank you for your time and consideration. (new paragraph) Sincerely, Yara Al-Harbi, Grade 7B","_w":{"checklist":["I used a formal greeting with the principal's title and family name.","My first paragraph says what I propose and why.","I gave specific details: who, when, where and cost.","I explained at least two benefits for students or the community.","I made a polite request (Would it be possible… / I would be grateful if…).","I used no contractions, idioms, slang or emojis.","I ended with thanks, Sincerely, and my full name and class.","My letter is 150–200 words, and I checked spelling and punctuation."],"min":150,"max":220}}]}],"game":{"name":"School Council Vote","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Council chamber: the child presents a proposal by choosing the best purpose, detail, benefit and request sentences; council members ask a question and the child picks the best formal answer. Three approvals = project launched.","Five students form the School Council.","Each 'proposer' reads the purpose and benefits paragraphs of his or her letter.","A council member asks one question from the question cards.","The proposer answers formally and politely.","The council votes; approved projects earn 3 points, and the best answer to a question earns 2 bonus points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What does a *proposal letter* do?","answer":"suggests a new project and asks for approval","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"يقترح مشروعًا ويطلب الموافقة.","options":["tells a funny story","describes a holiday","suggests a new project and asks for approval","lists the school rules"],"dok":1,"skill":"genre"},{"q":"What is *permission*?","answer":"the act of allowing someone to do something","explanation":"Vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"الإذن.","options":["a kind of fundraiser","a school subject","the act of allowing someone to do something","a type of letter"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*Kindness Week can reduce **loneliness**.* *Loneliness* means ___.","answer":"the sad feeling of being alone","explanation":"Context.","explanation_ar":"الوحدة.","options":["a kind of game","a school trip","a lot of noise","the sad feeling of being alone"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"What should the FIRST paragraph of your proposal letter include?","answer":"what you propose and why","explanation":"Structure.","explanation_ar":"ما تقترحه ولماذا.","options":["what you propose and why","your signature","only the cost","a joke"],"dok":1,"skill":"letter structure"},{"q":"Which sentence for a proposal letter is correct?","answer":"Students would collect the books in January.","explanation":"would + base verb.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Students would collected the books in January.","Students would collecting the books in January.","Students would to collect the books in January.","Students would collect the books in January."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which of these is a BENEFIT, not a detail?","answer":"Children in the hospital would have new books to enjoy.","explanation":"Benefit vs. detail.","explanation_ar":"فائدة.","options":["Children in the hospital would have new books to enjoy.","The fair would be on February 12.","Books would cost five riyals.","It would be in the school hall."],"dok":2,"skill":"benefits"},{"q":"Which sign-off is correct for your formal letter?","answer":"Sincerely, Yara Al-Harbi, Grade 7B","explanation":"Closing.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Bye bye! 😊","Love, Yara","Sincerely, Yara Al-Harbi, Grade 7B","See ya, Yara"],"dok":2,"skill":"letter format"},{"q":"Why should a proposal letter include specific numbers and dates?","answer":"They show that the plan is realistic and well prepared.","explanation":"Persuasion.","explanation_ar":"تُظهر أن الخطة واقعية.","options":["They make the letter funny.","They show that the plan is realistic and well prepared.","They replace the greeting.","They hide the request."],"dok":2,"skill":"details"},{"q":"A partner's letter says *We'll do it, it'll be fun, pls say yes!* What is the BEST advice?","answer":"Rewrite it in a formal tone with specific details and a polite request.","explanation":"Revising.","explanation_ar":"أسلوب رسمي وتفاصيل وطلب مهذب.","options":["Add more exclamation marks.","Make it shorter.","Add emojis.","Rewrite it in a formal tone with specific details and a polite request."],"dok":3,"skill":"revising"},{"q":"How does writing a proposal letter connect to the unit's theme of making a difference?","answer":"It turns a good idea into an organized plan that leaders can approve and support.","explanation":"Theme connection.","explanation_ar":"يحوّل الفكرة إلى خطة منظمة.","options":["It replaces the need for volunteers.","It turns a good idea into an organized plan that leaders can approve and support.","It is only practice for spelling.","It shows that ideas don't need planning."],"dok":3,"skill":"theme"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'charity': a box labeled DONATIONS"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'resident': elderly people smiling in a common room"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'care home': a calm building with a garden and benches"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'permission': a signed form with a check mark"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'supplier': a delivery van with boxes"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'loneliness': a child sitting alone on a bench"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'vote': hands raised in a classroom"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-01","prompt":"A class School Council voting on proposals."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-02","prompt":"Four school project planning cards."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L06-U6-LS5-03","prompt":"An envelope-shaped proposal planner."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V01","script":"charity. The book fair is a charity event."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V02","script":"resident. The residents of the care home enjoyed the visit."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V03","script":"care home. We visited a care home in our city."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V04","script":"permission. We need permission to use the hall."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V05","script":"supplier. The supplier's price is 4,000 riyals."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V06","script":"loneliness. Kindness Week can reduce loneliness."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-V07","script":"vote. The class council will vote on the proposals."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-T1","script":"**Card A – Water Refill Station** · What: a water refill station near the canteen · Why: students buy many small plastic bottles every day; a station would reduce plastic waste and keep students drinking water · Cost: about 4,000 riyals (supplier's price) · How to pay: a recycling drive and a class fundraiser · Who: the Eco Club (25 members) · When: ready before the hot season in April **Card B – Charity Book Fair** · What: a one-day fair selling donated used books for 5 riyals each · Why: money will buy new books for the children's library at the local hospital; students will also find books to read · Where: the school hall · When: Thursday, February 12, from 12:00 to 3:00 · Who: Grade 7 volunteers (30 students) and two teachers · Needs: permission to use the hall and to send a letter to parents asking for books **Card C – Elderly Visit Day** · What: a visit to a local care home for elderly people · Why: many residents rarely have visitors; students can read, talk and share Arabic coffee and dates with them · Who: 20 students from Grade 7 with three teachers · When: a Tuesday morning in March · Needs: permission, the school bus and parents' signed forms **Card D – Kindness Week** · What: a week of kindness activities: a compliment wall, a buddy bench in the playground and older students helping younger ones at lunch · Why: to make every student feel welcome and to reduce loneliness · When: the first week of the second term · Needs: permission and a small budget of 300 riyals for materials"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L06-U6-LS5-VID","script":"You have an idea that could make a difference. Now – how do you get the principal to say yes? A refill station, a charity book fair, a visit to a care home, a Kindness Week – which project will you propose? Dear Ms. Al-Otaibi, I am writing on behalf of Grade 7 to propose a Charity Book Fair… Purpose. Details and benefits. A polite request. Formal from 'Dear' to 'Sincerely'! Send your letter to our class School Council – and let the vote begin!"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Every ___ has the right to vote and the duty to care for the country.","answer":"citizen","explanation":"Citizen.","explanation_ar":"مواطن.","options":["fundraiser","target","railing","citizen"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"The school started a ___ to encourage students to walk or take the bus.","answer":"campaign","explanation":"Campaign.","explanation_ar":"حملة.","options":["campaign","budget","planter","herb"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Helping children with cancer is a ___ that many families support.","answer":"cause","explanation":"Cause.","explanation_ar":"قضية.","options":["railing","subject line","cause","contraction"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"The art club ___ a meeting to plan the charity exhibition.","answer":"organized","explanation":"Organize.","explanation_ar":"نظّم.","options":["donated","organized","swallowed","approved"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Our ___ is to collect 400 coats before the end of December.","answer":"target","explanation":"Target.","explanation_ar":"هدفنا.","options":["citizen","cause","target","permission"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*Everyone **pitched in**, and the hall was ready in half an hour.* What does *pitched in* mean?","answer":"joined in and helped","explanation":"Idiom.","explanation_ar":"شاركوا وساعدوا.","options":["threw balls","joined in and helped","complained","left early"],"dok":2,"skill":"idioms","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which idiom means *do more than you have to*?","answer":"go the extra mile","explanation":"Idiom.","explanation_ar":"go the extra mile.","options":["go the extra mile","lend a hand","every little bit helps","give back"],"dok":2,"skill":"idioms","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*Students, parents and teachers **collaborated** on the coat drive.* *Collaborated* means ___.","answer":"worked together","explanation":"Context.","explanation_ar":"تعاونوا.","options":["argued","competed","waited","worked together"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary in context","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which greeting is correct for a formal letter to the principal, Mr. Hamad Al-Zahrani?","answer":"Dear Mr. Al-Zahrani,","explanation":"Formal greeting.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Dear Mr. Al-Zahrani,","Hi Hamad!","Hey Principal!","Dear Hamad Al-Zahrani!!!"],"dok":1,"skill":"letter format","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"In a formal letter, which word should replace *pitch in*?","answer":"participate","explanation":"Formal language.","explanation_ar":"participate.","options":["chill","lend a hand","jump in","participate"],"dok":1,"skill":"formal language","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence is the BEST purpose sentence for a proposal letter?","answer":"I am writing to propose a coat drive for families in need in our city.","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"أفضل جملة غرض.","options":["Coats are warm.","I am writing to propose a coat drive for families in need in our city.","Winter is cold, you know.","We want to do stuff in winter."],"dok":2,"skill":"letter structure","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which polite request is written correctly?","answer":"Would it be possible to place a collection box near the entrance?","explanation":"Polite request.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Would it be possible place a collection box near the entrance?","Would it be possible to place a collection box near the entrance?","Would it possible to place a collection box near the entrance?","Would it be possibly to place a collection box near the entrance?"],"dok":2,"skill":"polite requests","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence states a THEME, not a topic?","answer":"Small acts of kindness can change someone's life.","explanation":"Theme vs. topic.","explanation_ar":"فكرة عامة.","options":["a coat drive","food banks","Small acts of kindness can change someone's life.","winter in Tabuk"],"dok":2,"skill":"theme","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"A student's letter ends *That's all! Bye! 😊* What is the BEST advice?","answer":"End with thanks, *Sincerely,* and your full name and class.","explanation":"Revising.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة رسمية.","options":["Add more emojis.","Delete the request.","Start the letter with this ending.","End with thanks, *Sincerely,* and your full name and class."],"dok":3,"skill":"revising","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"}],"unit_writing":{"task":"Write a formal letter (150–200 words) to your principal, Mr. Al-Zahrani, proposing a school food drive to collect canned and dry food for a local food bank. After a formal greeting, write three paragraphs: (1) what you propose and why; (2) specific details (who, when, where, how) and the benefits; (3) a polite request for approval, an offer to answer questions and thanks. End with a formal closing and your name and class.","model":"Dear Mr. Al-Zahrani, (new paragraph) I am writing on behalf of Grade 7A to propose a two-week food drive at our school. According to the United Nations, roughly one third of the world's food is lost or wasted, while some families in our own city struggle to buy enough to eat. (new paragraph) We would place three labeled collection boxes near the main entrance from March 1 to March 14. Students and families would donate unopened canned and dry food, such as rice, lentils, pasta and canned beans. Twenty volunteers from our class would sort the food every afternoon, and Ms. Huda, our science teacher, has agreed to supervise. At the end of the drive, a local food bank would collect everything. In addition to helping families in need, the project would raise awareness about food waste. (new paragraph) I would be grateful if you could approve this project and allow us to announce it at the morning assembly. I would be happy to answer any questions. Thank you for your time and consideration. (new paragraph) Sincerely, Bader Al-Anazi, Grade 7A","marks":20}});
